window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2"]={"id":"CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2","title":"CGL 23 OCT 2026 SHIFT 2","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000075081","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"Directions: Study the following information to answer the given questions:<br>'A + C' means 'A is the son of C',<br>'A - C' means 'A is the wife of C',<br>'A + C' means 'A is the father of C',<br>'A × C' means 'A is the sister of C',<br>If S + H × R - A + B + K, then<br>How is S related to A? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निर्देश: दी गई जानकारी के आधार पर प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए:<br>'A + C' का अर्थ 'A, C का पुत्र है',<br>'A - C' का अर्थ 'A, C की पत्नी है',<br>'A + C' का अर्थ 'A, C का पिता है',<br>'A × C' का अर्थ 'A, C की बहन है',<br>यदि S + H × R - A + B + K है, तो<br>S का A से क्या संबंध है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mother-in-law","hi":"सास"},"2":{"en":"Father-in-law","hi":"ससुर"},"3":{"en":"Mother","hi":"माता"},"4":{"en":"Father","hi":"पिता"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"S + H means S is the father of H, and H × R means H is the sister of R, so R is also a daughter of S<br>R - A means R is the wife of A, so A is the husband of S's daughter<br>Hence S is the father-in-law of A; the later part A + B + K only gives the father of A<br><svg width=\"280\" height=\"196\" viewBox=\"0 0 280 196\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M<path d=\"M130 85H214M130 91H214\"/><path d=\"M28 28V55H28V78\"/><path d=\"M28 28V55H124V78\"/><path d=\"M124 28V55H220V78\"/><path d=\"M124 28V55H220V144\"/><text x=\"124\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">B+</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">B+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">S+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">S+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">H−</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">H−</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">R−</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">R−</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A+</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A+</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">K+</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">K+</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></g></svg><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Father-in-law.</b>","hi":"S + H का अर्थ S, H का पिता है और H × R का अर्थ H, R की बहन है, अतः R भी S की पुत्री है<br>R - A का अर्थ R, A की पत्नी है, अतः A, S की पुत्री का पति है<br>इसलिए S, A का ससुर है; आगे A + B + K से केवल A के पिता का पता चलता है<br><svg width=\"280\" height=\"196\" viewBox=\"0 0 280 196\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M<path d=\"M130 85H214M130 91H214\"/><path d=\"M28 28V55H28V78\"/><path d=\"M28 28V55H124V78\"/><path d=\"M124 28V55H220V78\"/><path d=\"M124 28V55H220V144\"/><text x=\"124\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">B+</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">B+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">S+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">S+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">H−</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">H−</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">R−</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">R−</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A+</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A+</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">K+</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">K+</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></g></svg><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ससुर है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000075082","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Formation & Letter/Word Position","question":{"en":"In the following questions, select the word from the given alternatives which cannot be formed using the letters of the given word.<br><b>BRILLIANCE</b> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्नों में दिए गए विकल्पों से वह शब्द चुनिए जो दिए गए शब्द के अक्षरों से नहीं बनाया जा सकता।<br><b>BRILLIANCE</b> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"BRINE"},"2":{"en":"CRANE"},"3":{"en":"BALANCE"},"4":{"en":"NAIL"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"BRILLIANCE has the letters B, R, I, L, L, I, A, N, C, E<br>BRINE, CRANE and NAIL can all be taken from these letters<br>BALANCE needs two A's, but BRILLIANCE has only one A, so BALANCE cannot be formed<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): BALANCE.</b>","hi":"BRILLIANCE में अक्षर B, R, I, L, L, I, A, N, C, E हैं<br>BRINE, CRANE तथा NAIL इन सभी अक्षरों से बन सकते हैं<br>BALANCE में दो A चाहिए, परंतु BRILLIANCE में केवल एक A है, अतः BALANCE नहीं बन सकता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): BALANCE है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000075083","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"In the following question, two groups of letters are related by a specific pattern. Identify the same pattern and apply it to the second group to find the missing letters.<br>DARK : WZIP :: GLOW : ? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में अक्षरों के दो समूह एक विशिष्ट पैटर्न से संबंधित हैं। वही पैटर्न पहचानिए और दूसरे समूह पर लागू करके लुप्त अक्षर ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>DARK : WZIP :: GLOW : ? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"TLOD"},"2":{"en":"TOLD"},"3":{"en":"UPME"},"4":{"en":"UEPM"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Every letter is replaced by its opposite letter in the alphabet: D→W, A→Z, R→I, K→P<br>The same opposite letters of GLOW are G→T, L→O, O→L, W→D<br>So the answer is TOLD<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): TOLD.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक अक्षर को वर्णमाला में उसके विपरीत अक्षर से बदला जाता है: D→W, A→Z, R→I, K→P<br>GLOW के वही विपरीत अक्षर हैं G→T, L→O, O→L, W→D<br>अतः उत्तर TOLD है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): TOLD है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000075084","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Direction: In the question below, two statements are given, followed by two conclusions numbered I and II. You must assume everything in the statements to be true, then consider the two conclusions together and decide which of them logically follows beyond a reasonable doubt from the information given in the statements.<br><b>Statements:</b><br>1. Any student who attends the extra coaching program has an 80% chance of scoring above 75% in the final exams.<br>2. Roshan attended the extra coaching program this semester.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Roshan will score above 75% in his final exam.<br>II. Roshan has a high probability of scoring above 75% in his final exam. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निर्देश: नीचे दिए प्रश्न में दो कथन और उनके बाद I तथा II क्रमांकित दो निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथनों की सभी बातों को सत्य मानना है, फिर दोनों निष्कर्षों पर एक साथ विचार करके निर्णय कीजिए कि उनमें से कौन-सा कथनों की दी गई जानकारी से संदेह से परे तार्किक रूप से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>1. जो भी विद्यार्थी अतिरिक्त कोचिंग कार्यक्रम में भाग लेता है, उसके अंतिम परीक्षा में 75% से अधिक अंक पाने की 80% संभावना है।<br>2. रोशन ने इस सेमेस्टर अतिरिक्त कोचिंग कार्यक्रम में भाग लिया।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. रोशन अपनी अंतिम परीक्षा में 75% से अधिक अंक पाएगा।<br>II. रोशन के 75% से अधिक अंक पाने की उच्च संभावना है। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I follows","hi":"केवल I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only II follows","hi":"केवल II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both I and II follow","hi":"I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither follows","hi":"कोई नहीं निकलता"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"An 80% chance means the result is probable, not certain, so 'Roshan will score above 75%' cannot be concluded with certainty and I does not follow<br>That same 80% chance is exactly a high probability, so II follows<br>Hence only conclusion II follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Only II follows.</b>","hi":"80% संभावना का अर्थ है कि परिणाम संभावित है, निश्चित नहीं, अतः 'रोशन 75% से अधिक अंक पाएगा' निश्चित रूप से नहीं कहा जा सकता और I नहीं निकलता<br>वही 80% संभावना ही उच्च संभावना है, अतः II निकलता है<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): केवल II निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000075085","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"Find the missing number in the following series:<br>0, 3, 8, 15, 24, ?, 48 [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित श्रेणी में लुप्त संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए:<br>0, 3, 8, 15, 24, ?, 48 [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"32"},"2":{"en":"35"},"3":{"en":"38"},"4":{"en":"41"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The terms are of the form n² − 1 with n = 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7: 1 − 1 = 0, 4 − 1 = 3, 9 − 1 = 8, 16 − 1 = 15, 25 − 1 = 24<br>For n = 6 the term is 36 − 1 = 35 and for n = 7 it is 49 − 1 = 48 ✔<br>So the missing number is 35<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 35.</b>","hi":"पद n² − 1 के रूप में हैं जहाँ n = 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7: 1 − 1 = 0, 4 − 1 = 3, 9 − 1 = 8, 16 − 1 = 15, 25 − 1 = 24<br>n = 6 के लिए पद 36 − 1 = 35 तथा n = 7 के लिए 49 − 1 = 48 ✔<br>अतः लुप्त संख्या 35 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 35 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000075086","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"Find the missing number in the following series:<br>3, 4, 10, 33, 136, ? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित श्रेणी में लुप्त संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए:<br>3, 4, 10, 33, 136, ? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"525"},"2":{"en":"620"},"3":{"en":"655"},"4":{"en":"685"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Each term is multiplied by 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5 and then 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5 are added: 3 × 1 + 1 = 4, 4 × 2 + 2 = 10, 10 × 3 + 3 = 33, 33 × 4 + 4 = 136<br>Next term = 136 × 5 + 5 = 680 + 5 = 685<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 685.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पद को 1, 2, 3, 4 तथा 5 से गुणा करके 1, 2, 3, 4 तथा 5 जोड़े जाते हैं: 3 × 1 + 1 = 4, 4 × 2 + 2 = 10, 10 × 3 + 3 = 33, 33 × 4 + 4 = 136<br>अगला पद = 136 × 5 + 5 = 680 + 5 = 685<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 685 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000075087","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">63</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">52</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार किसी निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। इस पैटर्न को पहचानिए और उसके अनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">63</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">52</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"34"},"2":{"en":"44"},"3":{"en":"26"},"4":{"en":"52"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In every row the last number = first × second × third + third<br>4 × 5 × 3 + 3 = 60 + 3 = 63 ✔ and 2 × 6 × 4 + 4 = 48 + 4 = 52 ✔<br>Missing number = 3 × 4 × 2 + 2 = 24 + 2 = 26<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 26.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पंक्ति में अंतिम संख्या = पहली × दूसरी × तीसरी + तीसरी<br>4 × 5 × 3 + 3 = 60 + 3 = 63 ✔ तथा 2 × 6 × 4 + 4 = 48 + 4 = 52 ✔<br>लुप्त संख्या = 3 × 4 × 2 + 2 = 24 + 2 = 26<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 26 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000075088","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Select the odd number pair from the given alternatives. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दिए गए विकल्पों में से विषम संख्या युग्म चुनिए। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"31, 992"},"2":{"en":"27, 756"},"3":{"en":"14, 218"},"4":{"en":"16, 272"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Second number = first number × (first number + 1)<br>31 × 32 = 992 ✔, 27 × 28 = 756 ✔, 16 × 17 = 272 ✔<br>14 × 15 = 210, not 218 ✘<br>So 14, 218 is the odd pair<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 14, 218.</b>","hi":"दूसरी संख्या = पहली संख्या × (पहली संख्या + 1)<br>31 × 32 = 992 ✔, 27 × 28 = 756 ✔, 16 × 17 = 272 ✔<br>14 × 15 = 210 है, 218 नहीं ✘<br>अतः 14, 218 विषम युग्म है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 14, 218 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000075089","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"Select the correct option that replaces the asterisk sign (*) in the following equation.<br>14 * 2 * 8 * 4 * 2 = 16 [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित समीकरण में तारक चिह्न (*) के स्थान पर सही विकल्प चुनिए।<br>14 * 2 * 8 * 4 * 2 = 16 [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"+, ÷, −, −"},"2":{"en":"×, −, ÷, ÷"},"3":{"en":"÷, +, ×, ×"},"4":{"en":"+, ×, ÷, −"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Putting +, ×, ÷, − gives 14 + 2 × 8 ÷ 4 − 2<br>= 14 + 2 × 2 − 2 = 14 + 4 − 2 = 16 ✔<br>So the correct set of signs is +, ×, ÷, −<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): +, ×, ÷, −.</b>","hi":"+, ×, ÷, − रखने पर 14 + 2 × 8 ÷ 4 − 2 मिलता है<br>= 14 + 2 × 2 − 2 = 14 + 4 − 2 = 16 ✔<br>अतः चिह्नों का सही क्रम +, ×, ÷, − है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): +, ×, ÷, − है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000075090","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Choose the option which is exactly similar to: 22-04-2026, 33/A, Green Avenue, Model Town, Jalandhar-144003 [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"उस विकल्प का चयन कीजिए जो इससे पूर्णतः समान है: 22-04-2026, 33/A, Green Avenue, Model Town, Jalandhar-144003 [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"22-04-2026, 33-A, Green Avenue, Model Town, Jalandhar-144003"},"2":{"en":"22-04-2026, 33/A, Green Avenue, Model Town, Jalandhar-144003"},"3":{"en":"22-04-2026, 33/B, Green Avenue, Model Town, Jalandhar-144003"},"4":{"en":"24-02-2026, 33/A, Green Avenue, Model Town, Jalandhar-144003"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Option 1 writes 33-A instead of 33/A, option 3 writes 33/B and option 4 changes the date to 24-02-2026<br>Only option 2 repeats the date, house number, street, locality and PIN exactly<br>So option 2 is exactly similar to the given address<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 22-04-2026, 33/A, Green Avenue, Model Town, Jalandhar-144003.</b>","hi":"विकल्प 1 में 33/A के स्थान पर 33-A है, विकल्प 3 में 33/B है और विकल्प 4 में तारीख 24-02-2026 हो गई है<br>केवल विकल्प 2 तारीख, मकान संख्या, गली, क्षेत्र तथा पिन ठीक दोहराता है<br>अतः विकल्प 2 दिए पते से पूर्णतः समान है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 22-04-2026, 33/A, Green Avenue, Model Town, Jalandhar-144003 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000075091","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>In Kerala, a large number of dishes are prepared using coconut oil.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Coconut oil is the primary cooking oil used throughout the country.<br>II. Kerala consumes a significant amount of coconut oil. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए दो निष्कर्षों को देखिए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा निष्कर्ष तार्किक रूप से कथन से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>केरल में बड़ी संख्या में व्यंजन नारियल तेल से बनाए जाते हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. नारियल तेल पूरे देश में प्रयोग होने वाला प्रमुख खाना पकाने का तेल है।<br>II. केरल में नारियल तेल की खपत उल्लेखनीय मात्रा में होती है। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Both Conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II निकलता है"},"4":{"en":"Only Conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The statement speaks only about Kerala, so nothing can be said about the whole country and I does not follow<br>If a large number of dishes in Kerala use coconut oil, then Kerala certainly consumes a significant amount of it, so II follows<br>Hence only conclusion II follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Only Conclusion II follows.</b>","hi":"कथन केवल केरल के बारे में है, अतः पूरे देश के बारे में कुछ नहीं कहा जा सकता और I नहीं निकलता<br>यदि केरल में बड़ी संख्या में व्यंजन नारियल तेल से बनते हैं, तो केरल में उसकी खपत निश्चित रूप से उल्लेखनीय है, अतः II निकलता है<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000075092","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"In the following question a statement is given followed by some assumptions. Read the assumptions carefully and choose the appropriate option.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>Please verify all customer complaints before forwarding them to the management.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. Some customer complaints may not be genuine.<br>II. Management should receive only verified information. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन और उसके बाद कुछ अनुमान दिए गए हैं। अनुमानों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उपयुक्त विकल्प चुनिए।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>कृपया सभी ग्राहक शिकायतों को प्रबंधन को भेजने से पहले सत्यापित करें।<br><b>अनुमान:</b><br>I. कुछ ग्राहक शिकायतें वास्तविक नहीं हो सकतीं।<br>II. प्रबंधन को केवल सत्यापित जानकारी ही मिलनी चाहिए। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I is implicit.","hi":"केवल I निहित है।"},"2":{"en":"Only II is implicit.","hi":"केवल II निहित है।"},"3":{"en":"Neither I nor II is implicit.","hi":"न तो I और न ही II निहित है।"},"4":{"en":"Both I and II are implicit.","hi":"I और II दोनों निहित हैं।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Verification is asked for because some complaints may be false, so I is implicit<br>The instruction also assumes that management must act only on checked information, so II is implicit<br>Hence both assumptions are implicit<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Both I and II are implicit..</b>","hi":"सत्यापन इसलिए कहा गया है क्योंकि कुछ शिकायतें झूठी हो सकती हैं, अतः I निहित है<br>निर्देश यह भी मानता है कि प्रबंधन को केवल जाँची गई जानकारी ही मिलनी चाहिए, अतः II निहित है<br>इसलिए दोनों अनुमान निहित हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): I और II दोनों निहित हैं। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000075093","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"In the following question, one statement is given, followed by certain inferences. Consider the statement to be true even if it seems to contradict commonly known facts. Read the inferences carefully and decide which of them logically follow from the given statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>Residents of a particular locality have widely protested, alleging that the inquiry commission's report on the riot in their area was biased and not prepared fairly and impartially.<br><b>Inferences:</b><br>I. A fresh inquiry commission should be appointed to conduct an impartial and thorough investigation into the matter.<br>II. The members of the commission should be severely punished. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन और उसके बाद कुछ अनुमान दिए गए हैं। कथन को सत्य मानिए, भले ही वह सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों के विपरीत प्रतीत हो। अनुमानों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि उनमें से कौन-से तार्किक रूप से कथन से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>एक विशेष इलाके के निवासियों ने व्यापक विरोध किया है और आरोप लगाया है कि उनके क्षेत्र में हुए दंगे पर जाँच आयोग की रिपोर्ट पक्षपाती थी तथा निष्पक्ष और ईमानदारी से नहीं बनाई गई।<br><b>अनुमान:</b><br>I. मामले की निष्पक्ष और गहन जाँच के लिए नया जाँच आयोग नियुक्त किया जाना चाहिए।<br>II. आयोग के सदस्यों को कड़ी सज़ा दी जानी चाहिए। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Inference I follows.","hi":"केवल अनुमान I निकलता है।"},"2":{"en":"Only Inference II follows.","hi":"केवल अनुमान II निकलता है।"},"3":{"en":"Both Inferences I and II follow.","hi":"अनुमान I और II दोनों निकलते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Neither Inference I nor Inference II follows.","hi":"न तो अनुमान I और न ही अनुमान II निकलता है।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The statement only reports the residents' allegation, and an allegation does not establish that the report was biased<br>So neither a fresh commission nor punishment of the members can be inferred with certainty, and neither inference follows<br>Hence neither inference I nor II follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Neither Inference I nor Inference II follows..</b>","hi":"कथन केवल निवासियों के आरोप को बताता है और आरोप से यह सिद्ध नहीं होता कि रिपोर्ट पक्षपाती थी<br>अतः न नया आयोग बनाना और न सदस्यों को सज़ा देना निश्चित रूप से निकलता है<br>इसलिए न तो I और न ही II निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): न तो अनुमान I और न ही अनुमान II निकलता है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000075094","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If '★' means +, '♦' means −, '○' means ×, and '△' means ÷, find [(20 △ 5) ★ (6 ○ 2)] ♦ [(9 △ 3) ○ 4]. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि '★' का अर्थ +, '♦' का अर्थ −, '○' का अर्थ × और '△' का अर्थ ÷ है, तो [(20 △ 5) ★ (6 ○ 2)] ♦ [(9 △ 3) ○ 4] का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2"},"2":{"en":"4"},"3":{"en":"6"},"4":{"en":"8"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"First bracket: (20 ÷ 5) + (6 × 2) = 4 + 12 = 16<br>Second bracket: (9 ÷ 3) × 4 = 3 × 4 = 12<br>Now 16 − 12 = 4<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 4.</b>","hi":"पहला कोष्ठक: (20 ÷ 5) + (6 × 2) = 4 + 12 = 16<br>दूसरा कोष्ठक: (9 ÷ 3) × 4 = 3 × 4 = 12<br>अब 16 − 12 = 4<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 4 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000075095","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"In the following question, one statement is given, followed by certain inferences. Consider the statement to be true even if it seems to contradict commonly known facts. Read the inferences carefully and decide which of them logically follow from the given statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>The central bank has increased interest rates multiple times over the past year to control inflation, even though this has slowed credit growth in the economy.<br><b>Inferences:</b><br>I. Inflation control is a priority over credit expansion for the central bank.<br>II. Higher interest rates discourage borrowing.<br>III. Inflation has been eliminated in the economy. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन और उसके बाद कुछ अनुमान दिए गए हैं। कथन को सत्य मानिए, भले ही वह सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों के विपरीत प्रतीत हो। अनुमानों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि उनमें से कौन-से तार्किक रूप से कथन से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>केंद्रीय बैंक ने मुद्रास्फीति नियंत्रित करने के लिए पिछले वर्ष में कई बार ब्याज दरें बढ़ाई हैं, भले ही इससे अर्थव्यवस्था में ऋण वृद्धि धीमी हुई है।<br><b>अनुमान:</b><br>I. केंद्रीय बैंक के लिए मुद्रास्फीति नियंत्रण, ऋण विस्तार से अधिक प्राथमिकता है।<br>II. अधिक ब्याज दरें उधार लेने को हतोत्साहित करती हैं।<br>III. अर्थव्यवस्था में मुद्रास्फीति समाप्त हो गई है। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Inference I follows.","hi":"केवल अनुमान I निकलता है।"},"2":{"en":"Only Inferences I and III follow.","hi":"केवल अनुमान I और III निकलते हैं।"},"3":{"en":"Only Inference III follows.","hi":"केवल अनुमान III निकलता है।"},"4":{"en":"Only Inferences I and II follow.","hi":"केवल अनुमान I और II निकलते हैं।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The bank accepted slower credit growth in order to control inflation, which shows that inflation control was given priority, so I follows<br>Rates were raised to reduce borrowing, i.e. higher rates discourage borrowing, so II follows<br>'Control inflation' does not mean inflation was eliminated, so III does not follow<br>Hence only inferences I and II follow<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Only Inferences I and II follow..</b>","hi":"बैंक ने मुद्रास्फीति नियंत्रित करने के लिए ऋण वृद्धि धीमी होने को स्वीकार किया, जिससे स्पष्ट है कि मुद्रास्फीति नियंत्रण को प्राथमिकता दी गई, अतः I निकलता है<br>दरें उधार घटाने के लिए बढ़ाई गईं, अर्थात अधिक दरें उधार लेने को हतोत्साहित करती हैं, अतः II निकलता है<br>'मुद्रास्फीति नियंत्रित करना' का अर्थ मुद्रास्फीति समाप्त होना नहीं, अतः III नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए केवल अनुमान I और II निकलते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): केवल अनुमान I और II निकलते हैं। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000075096","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Course of Action","question":{"en":"A manager must deny a remote work-flexibility request from a highly respected, top-performing employee because granting it would violate strict operational constraints and create severe equity and fairness concerns for the rest of the team. The employee is visibly disappointed upon hearing the denial but remains professional and respectful.<br>What course of action by the manager demonstrates the highest level of emotional intelligence (EQ)? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक प्रबंधक को एक अत्यंत सम्मानित, शीर्ष प्रदर्शन करने वाले कर्मचारी के दूर से काम करने की लचीलापन माँगने के अनुरोध को अस्वीकार करना पड़ता है, क्योंकि उसे स्वीकार करना कड़ी परिचालन बाधाओं का उल्लंघन होगा और शेष टीम के लिए समानता तथा निष्पक्षता की गंभीर समस्याएँ पैदा करेगा। अस्वीकृति सुनकर कर्मचारी स्पष्ट रूप से निराश है परंतु व्यावसायिक और सम्मानजनक बना हुआ है।<br>प्रबंधक की कौन-सी कार्यवाही सर्वोच्च भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता (EQ) दर्शाती है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Reverse the denial immediately, assuming top performers deserve special exemptions from team-wide standards.","hi":"शीर्ष प्रदर्शन करने वाले विशेष छूट के पात्र होते हैं, यह मानकर अस्वीकृति तुरंत वापस ले लें।"},"2":{"en":"Enforce the denial abruptly without providing any strategic explanation to prevent debate or negotiation.","hi":"बहस या सौदेबाज़ी रोकने के लिए बिना कोई रणनीतिक स्पष्टीकरण दिए अस्वीकृति अचानक लागू कर दें।"},"3":{"en":"Postpone delivering the definitive decision indefinitely to avoid immediate discomfort and protect the relationship.","hi":"तुरंत असुविधा से बचने और संबंध बचाने के लिए अंतिम निर्णय अनिश्चितकाल के लिए टाल दें।"},"4":{"en":"Explain the operational constraints transparently, validate their disappointment with empathy, and collaboratively explore alternatives.","hi":"परिचालन बाधाएँ पारदर्शी रूप से समझाएँ, उनकी निराशा को सहानुभूति से स्वीकारें और मिलकर विकल्प खोजें।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"A fair decision has to stay, so reversing it would break the standards for the whole team<br>Explaining the constraints honestly, accepting the disappointment and looking for alternatives together keeps both fairness and the relationship intact<br>Abrupt enforcement or endless postponement harms trust, so the last option is the emotionally intelligent one<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Explain the operational constraints transparently, validate their disappointment with empathy, and collaboratively explore alternatives..</b>","hi":"निष्पक्ष निर्णय बना रहना चाहिए, अतः उसे वापस लेना पूरी टीम के मानक तोड़ देगा<br>बाधाएँ ईमानदारी से समझाना, निराशा स्वीकारना और मिलकर विकल्प खोजना निष्पक्षता तथा संबंध दोनों बनाए रखता है<br>अचानक लागू करना या अनिश्चितकाल तक टालना विश्वास को हानि पहुँचाता है, अतः अंतिम विकल्प भावनात्मक रूप से बुद्धिमान है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): परिचालन बाधाएँ पारदर्शी रूप से समझाएँ, उनकी निराशा को सहानुभूति से स्वीकारें और मिलकर विकल्प खोजें। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000075097","section":"REASONING","topic":"Matrix","question":{"en":"Which of the following rows/columns are connected/related with each other in some way?<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Rows</td><td colspan=\"5\" style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px;text-align:center\">Columns</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">14</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">20</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">24</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">13</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">28</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी पंक्तियाँ/स्तंभ किसी प्रकार एक-दूसरे से जुड़े/संबंधित हैं?<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Rows</td><td colspan=\"5\" style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px;text-align:center\">Columns</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">14</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">20</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">24</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">13</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">28</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Columns I, II and V","hi":"स्तंभ I, II और V"},"2":{"en":"Columns I, II and IV","hi":"स्तंभ I, II और IV"},"3":{"en":"Columns II, III and IV","hi":"स्तंभ II, III और IV"},"4":{"en":"Columns III, IV and V","hi":"स्तंभ III, IV और V"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Column II is three times column I: 2 × 3 = 6, 4 × 3 = 12, 3 × 3 = 9, 5 × 3 = 15, 6 × 3 = 18<br>Column V is two times column I: 2 × 2 = 4, 4 × 2 = 8, 3 × 2 = 6, 5 × 2 = 10, 6 × 2 = 12<br>So columns I, II and V are related to one another<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Columns I, II and V.</b>","hi":"स्तंभ II, स्तंभ I का तीन गुना है: 2 × 3 = 6, 4 × 3 = 12, 3 × 3 = 9, 5 × 3 = 15, 6 × 3 = 18<br>स्तंभ V, स्तंभ I का दो गुना है: 2 × 2 = 4, 4 × 2 = 8, 3 × 2 = 6, 5 × 2 = 10, 6 × 2 = 12<br>अतः स्तंभ I, II और V परस्पर संबंधित हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): स्तंभ I, II और V है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000075098","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"BUILDING\" is written as \"2uilDI14G\". How will \"HARMONIC\" be written in the same code language? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"किसी निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"BUILDING\" को \"2uilDI14G\" लिखा जाता है। उसी कूट भाषा में \"HARMONIC\" को कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8arMON8C"},"2":{"en":"8aRMON9C"},"3":{"en":"8ARMON9C"},"4":{"en":"8arMON9C"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In BUILDING the first letter B is written as its alphabet position 2, the 2nd, 3rd and 4th letters U, I, L become small letters and the 7th letter N is written as its position 14, all other letters staying the same: B U I L D I N G → 2 u i l D I 14 G<br>HARMONIC gives H = 8, a r m in small letters, O and N unchanged, I = 9 and C unchanged<br>So the code is 8armON9C, printed in option 4 as 8arMON9C with a capital M<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 8arMON9C.</b>","hi":"BUILDING में पहला अक्षर B अपने वर्णमाला स्थान 2 के रूप में, दूसरा, तीसरा और चौथा अक्षर U, I, L छोटे अक्षरों में तथा सातवाँ अक्षर N अपने स्थान 14 के रूप में लिखा जाता है, शेष अक्षर वही रहते हैं: B U I L D I N G → 2 u i l D I 14 G<br>HARMONIC से H = 8, a r m छोटे अक्षरों में, O और N अपरिवर्तित, I = 9 तथा C अपरिवर्तित<br>अतः कूट 8armON9C है, जो विकल्प 4 में 8arMON9C (बड़े M के साथ) छपा है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 8arMON9C है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000075099","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the following question two statements are given and these statements are followed by two conclusions. You have to take the given two statements to be true even if they seem to be at variance from commonly known facts. Read the conclusions and then decide which of the given conclusions logically follows from the two given statements.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>Some dreams are nights.<br>Some nights are days.<br><b>Conclusion:</b><br>I. All days are nights.<br>II. Some days are nights. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में दो कथन और उनके बाद दो निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। दिए गए दोनों कथनों को सत्य मानना है, भले ही वे सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों से भिन्न प्रतीत हों। निष्कर्षों को पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा निष्कर्ष दिए गए दोनों कथनों से तार्किक रूप से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>कुछ सपने रातें हैं।<br>कुछ रातें दिन हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. सभी दिन रातें हैं।<br>II. कुछ दिन रातें हैं। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I अनुसरण करता है"},"2":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों अनुसरण करते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor conclusion II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II अनुसरण करता है"},"4":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II अनुसरण करता है"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"'Some nights are days' converts to 'some days are nights', so II follows<br>'All days are nights' is only a possibility and not certain, so I does not follow<br>Hence only conclusion II follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Only conclusion II follows.</b>","hi":"'कुछ रातें दिन हैं' से 'कुछ दिन रातें हैं' प्राप्त होता है, अतः II अनुसरण करता है<br>'सभी दिन रातें हैं' केवल संभावना है, निश्चित नहीं, अतः I अनुसरण नहीं करता<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष II अनुसरण करता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): केवल निष्कर्ष II अनुसरण करता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000075100","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"After submitting an important assignment that contributes significantly to the final grade, a student carefully reviews a copy of the work and discovers several factual and calculation errors that could affect the accuracy of the submission. The assignment has not yet been graded, and the student must decide how to respond in a manner that reflects academic integrity and responsibility.<br>What should the student do? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"अंतिम ग्रेड में महत्वपूर्ण योगदान देने वाला एक महत्वपूर्ण असाइनमेंट जमा करने के बाद एक विद्यार्थी उसकी प्रति की सावधानी से समीक्षा करता है और पाता है कि उसमें कई तथ्यात्मक तथा गणना संबंधी त्रुटियाँ हैं जो प्रस्तुति की सटीकता को प्रभावित कर सकती हैं। असाइनमेंट अभी जाँचा नहीं गया है और विद्यार्थी को ऐसे उत्तर देने का निर्णय लेना है जो शैक्षणिक ईमानदारी तथा उत्तरदायित्व दर्शाए।<br>विद्यार्थी को क्या करना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ignore the errors and hope they go unnoticed during evaluation.","hi":"त्रुटियों को अनदेखा करें और आशा करें कि मूल्यांकन में वे ध्यान में न आएँ।"},"2":{"en":"Promptly notify the instructor about the mistakes and seek guidance on whether corrections can be submitted.","hi":"शीघ्र शिक्षक को त्रुटियों के बारे में सूचित करें और मार्गदर्शन लें कि सुधार जमा किए जा सकते हैं या नहीं।"},"3":{"en":"Attribute responsibility for the errors to classmates who were not involved in preparing the assignment.","hi":"त्रुटियों का दोष उन सहपाठियों पर डालें जो असाइनमेंट बनाने में शामिल नहीं थे।"},"4":{"en":"Attempt to remove or conceal any evidence that the mistakes were made.","hi":"इस बात के सभी प्रमाण मिटाने या छिपाने का प्रयास करें कि त्रुटियाँ हुई थीं।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Academic integrity means admitting one's own mistakes before they are evaluated<br>Informing the instructor and asking about corrections is honest and gives the instructor a fair chance to decide<br>Ignoring the errors, blaming others or hiding evidence only damages trust and learning<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Promptly notify the instructor about the mistakes and seek guidance on whether corrections can be submitted..</b>","hi":"शैक्षणिक ईमानदारी का अर्थ है मूल्यांकन से पहले अपनी त्रुटियाँ स्वीकार करना<br>शिक्षक को सूचित करना और सुधार के बारे में पूछना ईमानदार है और शिक्षक को निर्णय का उचित अवसर देता है<br>त्रुटियाँ अनदेखा करना, दोष दूसरों पर डालना या प्रमाण छिपाना केवल विश्वास और सीख को हानि पहुँचाता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): शीघ्र शिक्षक को त्रुटियों के बारे में सूचित करें और मार्गदर्शन लें कि सुधार जमा किए जा सकते हैं या नहीं। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000075101","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"Read the given statement carefully and the following assumptions based on it. Decide which of the assumptions are implicit in the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>The agricultural department should subsidize organic farming techniques to encourage farmers to adopt more sustainable and eco-friendly methods of food production.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. Farmers are currently disincentivized from choosing organic methods due to higher initial costs.<br>II. Sustainable farming is a necessary step towards maintaining long-term food security and safety. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दिया गया कथन ध्यान से पढ़िए और उस पर आधारित अनुमानों को देखिए। निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-से अनुमान कथन में निहित हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>कृषि विभाग को जैविक खेती तकनीकों पर सब्सिडी देनी चाहिए ताकि किसान अधिक टिकाऊ और पर्यावरण-अनुकूल खाद्य उत्पादन विधियाँ अपनाएँ।<br><b>अनुमान:</b><br>I. अधिक प्रारंभिक लागत के कारण किसान इस समय जैविक विधियाँ चुनने से हतोत्साहित हैं।<br>II. दीर्घकालिक खाद्य सुरक्षा और सुरक्षितता बनाए रखने के लिए टिकाऊ खेती एक आवश्यक कदम है। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Assumption I is implicit","hi":"केवल अनुमान I निहित है"},"2":{"en":"Only Assumption II is implicit","hi":"केवल अनुमान II निहित है"},"3":{"en":"Neither Assumption I nor II is implicit","hi":"न तो अनुमान I और न ही II निहित है"},"4":{"en":"Both Assumptions I and II are implicit","hi":"अनुमान I और II दोनों निहित हैं"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"A subsidy is suggested because higher initial cost keeps farmers away from organic methods, so I is implicit<br>The statement asks for adoption of organic methods, which presupposes that it matters for long-term food production and safety, so II is also implicit<br>Hence both assumptions are implicit<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only Assumption I is implicit.</b>","hi":"सब्सिडी इसलिए सुझाई गई है क्योंकि अधिक प्रारंभिक लागत किसानों को जैविक विधियों से दूर रखती है, अतः I निहित है<br>कथन जैविक विधियाँ अपनाने को कहता है और इससे मान लिया जाता है कि यह दीर्घकालिक खाद्य उत्पादन तथा सुरक्षा के लिए महत्वपूर्ण है, अतः II भी निहित है<br>इसलिए दोनों अनुमान निहित हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल अनुमान I निहित है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000075102","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"An organisation promotes an employee to senior grade if they have ≥ 5 years in the current grade, no red flag in the last two annual reviews, and have cleared the departmental exam. Employees with ≥ 7 years but who have not cleared the exam instead get a financial upgradation only (no grade change).<br><b>Employee:</b> 6 years in grade, no red flags, exam not cleared. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक संगठन कर्मचारी को वरिष्ठ ग्रेड में पदोन्नत करता है यदि उनके पास वर्तमान ग्रेड में ≥ 5 वर्ष हैं, पिछले दो वार्षिक समीक्षाओं में कोई रेड फ्लैग नहीं है और उन्होंने विभागीय परीक्षा उत्तीर्ण की है। जिनके पास ≥ 7 वर्ष हैं परंतु परीक्षा उत्तीर्ण नहीं की, उन्हें ग्रेड परिवर्तन के बजाय केवल वित्तीय उन्नयन मिलता है।<br><b>कर्मचारी:</b> ग्रेड में 6 वर्ष, कोई रेड फ्लैग नहीं, परीक्षा उत्तीर्ण नहीं। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Promoted to senior grade","hi":"वरिष्ठ ग्रेड में पदोन्नत"},"2":{"en":"Financial upgradation only","hi":"केवल वित्तीय उन्नयन"},"3":{"en":"Not promoted, no upgradation","hi":"पदोन्नति नहीं, कोई उन्नयन नहीं"},"4":{"en":"Promoted automatically next cycle","hi":"अगले चक्र में स्वतः पदोन्नत"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Grade promotion needs both ≥ 5 years and the departmental exam, and the exam is not cleared, so promotion is ruled out<br>The financial upgradation needs ≥ 7 years, but the employee has only 6 years<br>So the employee is neither promoted nor given an upgradation<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Not promoted, no upgradation.</b>","hi":"ग्रेड पदोन्नति के लिए ≥ 5 वर्ष तथा विभागीय परीक्षा दोनों आवश्यक हैं और परीक्षा उत्तीर्ण नहीं है, अतः पदोन्नति नहीं हो सकती<br>वित्तीय उन्नयन के लिए ≥ 7 वर्ष चाहिए, परंतु कर्मचारी के पास केवल 6 वर्ष हैं<br>अतः कर्मचारी को न पदोन्नति मिलेगी और न उन्नयन<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): पदोन्नति नहीं, कोई उन्नयन नहीं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000075103","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"A credit card limit is automatically increased after 12 consecutive months of on-time payments with utilization below 30%. Conversely, a utilization of 30–50% with on-time payments triggers a manual review.<br><b>Scenario:</b> A cardholder has made 12 months of on-time payments and has a utilization of 35%. What is the outcome? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"12 लगातार महीनों तक समय पर भुगतान और 30% से कम उपयोग पर क्रेडिट कार्ड की सीमा स्वतः बढ़ा दी जाती है। इसके विपरीत, समय पर भुगतान के साथ 30–50% उपयोग होने पर मैनुअल समीक्षा शुरू होती है।<br><b>परिदृश्य:</b> एक कार्डधारक ने 12 महीने समय पर भुगतान किया है और उसका उपयोग 35% है। परिणाम क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Automatic limit increase","hi":"सीमा में स्वतः वृद्धि"},"2":{"en":"No change to the limit","hi":"सीमा में कोई परिवर्तन नहीं"},"3":{"en":"Limit is decreased","hi":"सीमा घटाई जाती है"},"4":{"en":"Manual review triggered","hi":"मैनुअल समीक्षा शुरू होती है"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Automatic increase needs utilization below 30%, but the utilization is 35%, so the automatic increase does not apply<br>A utilization between 30% and 50% with on-time payments triggers a manual review, which is exactly this case<br>So a manual review is triggered<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Manual review triggered.</b>","hi":"स्वतः वृद्धि के लिए उपयोग 30% से कम होना चाहिए, परंतु उपयोग 35% है, अतः स्वतः वृद्धि लागू नहीं होती<br>समय पर भुगतान के साथ 30% से 50% के बीच उपयोग मैनुअल समीक्षा शुरू करता है, और यही स्थिति यहाँ है<br>अतः मैनुअल समीक्षा शुरू होगी<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): मैनुअल समीक्षा शुरू होती है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000075104","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Which of the following letter-clusters will replace the question mark (?) in the given series to make it logically complete?<br>AM, CO, FR, JV, OA, ? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा अक्षर-समूह दी गई श्रेणी को तार्किक रूप से पूर्ण करने के लिए प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर आएगा?<br>AM, CO, FR, JV, OA, ? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"BN"},"2":{"en":"CN"},"3":{"en":"BO"},"4":{"en":"DO"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The two letters of each cluster are 12 places apart: A(1) and M(13), C(3) and O(15), F(6) and R(18), J(10) and V(22), O(15) and A(1 + 26)<br>The first letter moves ahead by 2, 3, 4 and 5 places, so the next step is +6; but no option carries the cluster that this gives, because the printed options do not continue the +2, +3, +4, +5 pattern<br>SSC has given this answer in the official answer key, so the key value BN is kept<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): BN.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक समूह के दोनों अक्षर 12 स्थान के अंतर पर हैं: A(1) और M(13), C(3) और O(15), F(6) और R(18), J(10) और V(22), O(15) और A(1 + 26)<br>पहला अक्षर 2, 3, 4 तथा 5 स्थान आगे बढ़ता है, अतः अगला कदम +6 है; परंतु मुद्रित विकल्प उस समूह को नहीं देते जो इस नियम से बनता है<br>SSC ने आधिकारिक उत्तर कुंजी में यही उत्तर दिया है, अतः कुंजी का मान BN ही रखा गया है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): BN है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000075105","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Observe the following pairs of alphanumeric codes carefully. In three options, the second code is obtained from the first by interchanging each of the characters at the 3rd and 9th positions, and the characters at the 5th and 11th positions, while all other characters remain unchanged.<br>Which option does not follow this transformation? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित अल्फ़ान्यूमेरिक कूटों के युग्मों को ध्यान से देखिए। तीन विकल्पों में दूसरा कूट पहले से तीसरे और नौवें स्थान के अक्षरों तथा पाँचवें और ग्यारहवें स्थान के अक्षरों को परस्पर बदलकर प्राप्त होता है, शेष सभी अक्षर अपरिवर्तित रहते हैं।<br>कौन-सा विकल्प इस रूपांतरण का पालन नहीं करता? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"K7M4P9R2T6V8 → K7T4V9R2M6P8"},"2":{"en":"Q3L8N5C7F2H6 → Q3F8H5C7L2N6"},"3":{"en":"B9D2G6K4M7R5 → B9M2R6K4D7G5"},"4":{"en":"W4E7J2P9S5U3 → W4S7S2P9EJU3"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Original code: W 4 E 7 J 2 P 9 S 5 U 3, so the 3rd character E and the 9th character S, and the 5th character J and the 11th character U, are to be interchanged<br>The correct second code must therefore be W 4 S 7 U 2 P 9 E 5 J 3<br>The printed second code of option 4 is shorter and repeats S and E in place of other characters, so it does not follow this transformation<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): W4E7J2P9S5U3 → W4S7S2P9EJU3.</b>","hi":"मूल कूट: W 4 E 7 J 2 P 9 S 5 U 3, अतः तीसरा अक्षर E और नौवाँ अक्षर S तथा पाँचवाँ अक्षर J और ग्यारहवाँ अक्षर U परस्पर बदलने चाहिए<br>इसलिए सही दूसरा कूट W 4 S 7 U 2 P 9 E 5 J 3 होना चाहिए<br>विकल्प 4 का मुद्रित दूसरा कूट छोटा है तथा अन्य अक्षरों के स्थान पर S और E दोहराता है, अतः यह इस रूपांतरण का पालन नहीं करता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): W4E7J2P9S5U3 → W4S7S2P9EJU3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000075106","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Dams, Lakes and Waterfall","question":{"en":"In which state are the 'Phumdis' (floating islands of decomposed plant materials) found? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"'फुमदी' (सड़े हुए पादप पदार्थों से बने तैरते द्वीप) किस राज्य में पाए जाते हैं? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Manipur","hi":"मणिपुर"},"2":{"en":"Mizoram","hi":"मिज़ोरम"},"3":{"en":"Tripura","hi":"त्रिपुरा"},"4":{"en":"Nagaland","hi":"नागालैंड"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Manipur</b><br><b>Phumdis</b> are heterogeneous masses of vegetation, soil and organic matter that float on the surface of <b>Loktak Lake in Manipur</b>, the largest freshwater lake of north-east India.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The largest phumdi, which hosts the <b>Keibul Lamjao National Park</b>, is the only floating national park in the world and the home of the <b>Sangai (brow-antlered deer)</b>, the state animal of Manipur.<br>• Phumdis form a unique wetland ecosystem that supports the livelihood of fisherfolk living in <b>phumshongs</b> (floating huts).<br>• Loktak Lake is a <b>Ramsar site</b> (designated 1990) and is fed by the Manipur River.<br>• <b>Mizoram, Tripura and Nagaland</b> are hilly states of the north-east, but phumdis are specific to Loktak in Manipur.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because phumdis are found in Manipur.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – मणिपुर</b><br><b>फुमदी (Phumdis)</b> वनस्पति, मिट्टी तथा कार्बनिक पदार्थ के विषमांगी पिंड हैं, जो पूर्वोत्तर भारत की सबसे बड़ी मीठे जल की झील <b>मणिपुर की लोकतक झील</b> की सतह पर तैरते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सबसे बड़ी फुमदी, जिस पर <b>केबुल लामजाओ राष्ट्रीय उद्यान</b> स्थित है, विश्व का एकमात्र तैरता राष्ट्रीय उद्यान है तथा <b>संगाई (भौंह-सींगी हिरण)</b> का घर है, जो मणिपुर का राज्य पशु है।<br>• फुमदी एक अनोखा आर्द्रभूमि पारिस्थितिकी तंत्र बनाते हैं, जो <b>फुमशोंग (तैरती झोपड़ियाँ)</b> में रहने वाले मछुआरों की आजीविका का सहारा हैं।<br>• लोकतक झील <b>रामसर स्थल</b> (1990 में नामित) है और इसे मणिपुर नदी से जल मिलता है।<br>• <b>मिज़ोरम, त्रिपुरा तथा नागालैंड</b> पूर्वोत्तर के पहाड़ी राज्य हैं, परंतु फुमदी मणिपुर की लोकतक झील तक ही सीमित हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि फुमदी मणिपुर में पाए जाते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000075107","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Motion","question":{"en":"When velocity is constant, what is the value of acceleration? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"जब वेग स्थिर होता है, तो त्वरण का मान क्या होता है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Maximum","hi":"अधिकतम"},"2":{"en":"Zero","hi":"शून्य"},"3":{"en":"Negative","hi":"ऋणात्मक"},"4":{"en":"Constant","hi":"स्थिर"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Zero</b><br>Acceleration is the rate of change of velocity; when velocity is <b>constant</b>, its change is zero and therefore <b>acceleration is zero</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• \\(a = \\frac{v - u}{t}\\); if \\(v = u\\), then \\(a = 0\\).<br>• The motion is then called <b>uniform motion</b>, and the velocity-time graph is a horizontal line.<br>• <b>Negative acceleration</b> (retardation) occurs when speed decreases, and a constant velocity cannot be maximum or negative by definition.<br>• An object can have zero acceleration even while moving, as in uniform circular motion with constant speed but there the velocity direction changes, so acceleration is not zero.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because constant velocity means zero acceleration.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – शून्य</b><br>त्वरण वेग परिवर्तन की दर है; जब वेग <b>स्थिर</b> होता है तो उसमें परिवर्तन शून्य होता है, इसलिए <b>त्वरण शून्य</b> होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• \\(a = \\frac{v - u}{t}\\); यदि \\(v = u\\) हो तो \\(a = 0\\)।<br>• ऐसी गति को <b>एकसमान गति (Uniform motion)</b> कहा जाता है और वेग-समय ग्राफ क्षैतिज रेखा होता है।<br>• <b>ऋणात्मक त्वरण</b> (मंदन) तब होता है जब चाल घटती है, तथा स्थिर वेग परिभाषा से अधिकतम या ऋणात्मक नहीं हो सकता।<br>• एकसमान वृत्तीय गति में चाल स्थिर होने पर भी त्वरण शून्य नहीं होता, क्योंकि वेग की दिशा बदलती है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि स्थिर वेग का अर्थ शून्य त्वरण है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000075108","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Gravitation and Work Done","question":{"en":"Mechanical energy is the sum of kinetic energy and which of the following forms of energy? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यांत्रिक ऊर्जा गतिज ऊर्जा तथा निम्नलिखित में से किस ऊर्जा का योग है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Heat energy only","hi":"केवल ऊष्मा ऊर्जा"},"2":{"en":"Chemical energy only","hi":"केवल रासायनिक ऊर्जा"},"3":{"en":"Potential energy only","hi":"केवल स्थितिज ऊर्जा"},"4":{"en":"Nuclear energy only","hi":"केवल नाभिकीय ऊर्जा"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Potential energy only</b><br><b>Mechanical energy</b> is the sum of <b>kinetic energy and potential energy</b> of a body, and in the absence of friction and other dissipative forces it remains constant.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• \\(E = \\frac{1}{2}mv^2 + mgh\\) – kinetic plus gravitational potential energy.<br>• Mechanical energy is <b>conserved</b> only when non-conservative forces such as friction do no work.<br>• Heat, chemical and nuclear energy are other forms of energy that are <b>not</b> part of mechanical energy.<br>• An object falling freely converts potential energy into kinetic energy while the total mechanical energy stays the same.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because mechanical energy = kinetic + potential energy.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – केवल स्थितिज ऊर्जा</b><br><b>यांत्रिक ऊर्जा (Mechanical energy)</b> किसी वस्तु की <b>गतिज ऊर्जा तथा स्थितिज ऊर्जा</b> का योग है, और घर्षण आदि क्षयकारी बलों की अनुपस्थिति में यह स्थिर रहती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• \\(E = \\frac{1}{2}mv^2 + mgh\\) – गतिज तथा गुरुत्वीय स्थितिज ऊर्जा।<br>• यांत्रिक ऊर्जा <b>संरक्षित</b> तभी रहती है जब घर्षण जैसे असंरक्षी बल कोई कार्य न करें।<br>• ऊष्मा, रासायनिक तथा नाभिकीय ऊर्जा ऊर्जा के अन्य रूप हैं, जो यांत्रिक ऊर्जा का भाग <b>नहीं</b> हैं।<br>• स्वतंत्र रूप से गिरती वस्तु स्थितिज ऊर्जा को गतिज ऊर्जा में बदलती है, जबकि कुल यांत्रिक ऊर्जा समान रहती है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि यांत्रिक ऊर्जा = गतिज + स्थितिज ऊर्जा।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000075109","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Preamble","question":{"en":"Which Supreme Court case held that the Preamble is a part of the Indian Constitution? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"किस सर्वोच्च न्यायालय मामले में यह अभिनिर्धारित हुआ कि प्रस्तावना भारतीय संविधान का भाग है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"S.R. Bommai Case","hi":"एस. आर. बोम्मई मामला"},"2":{"en":"Golaknath Case","hi":"गोलकनाथ मामला"},"3":{"en":"Berubari Union Case","hi":"बेरुबाड़ी संघ मामला"},"4":{"en":"Kesavananda Bharati Case","hi":"केशवानंद भारती मामला"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Kesavananda Bharati Case</b><br>In <b>Kesavananda Bharati v. State of Kerala (1973)</b> the Supreme Court overruled the earlier Berubari view and held that the <b>Preamble is a part of the Constitution</b> and can be used for interpretation.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• In the <b>Berubari Union case (1960)</b> the Court had said the Preamble is not a part of the Constitution but a key to the minds of the framers.<br>• In <b>LIC of India case (1995)</b> the Court reaffirmed that the Preamble is an integral part of the Constitution.<br>• Kesavananda Bharati also laid down the <b>basic structure doctrine</b> – Parliament cannot amend the basic features of the Constitution.<br>• <b>S.R. Bommai (1994)</b> dealt with Article 356, <b>Golaknath (1967)</b> with fundamental rights and <b>Berubari</b> with the Nehru-Noon Agreement on territory transfer.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because the Preamble's status as part of the Constitution was settled in the Kesavananda Bharati case.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – केशवानंद भारती मामला</b><br><b>केशवानंद भारती बनाम केरल राज्य (1973)</b> में सर्वोच्च न्यायालय ने बेरुबाड़ी के पूर्व मत को पलटते हुए अभिनिर्धारित किया कि <b>प्रस्तावना संविधान का भाग है</b> और इसका उपयोग संविधान की व्याख्या में किया जा सकता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>बेरुबाड़ी संघ मामले (1960)</b> में न्यायालय ने कहा था कि प्रस्तावना संविधान का भाग नहीं, बल्कि निर्माताओं के मन की कुंजी है।<br>• <b>भारतीय जीवन बीमा निगम मामले (1995)</b> में न्यायालय ने पुनः पुष्टि की कि प्रस्तावना संविधान का अभिन्न अंग है।<br>• केशवानंद भारती मामले में <b>आधारभूत संरचना सिद्धांत</b> भी दिया गया – संसद संविधान के मूल लक्षणों में संशोधन नहीं कर सकती।<br>• <b>एस. आर. बोम्मई (1994)</b> अनुच्छेद 356 से, <b>गोलकनाथ (1967)</b> मूल अधिकारों से तथा <b>बेरुबाड़ी</b> नेहरू-नून समझौते से संबंधित था।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि प्रस्तावना के संविधान का भाग होने का निर्णय केशवानंद भारती मामले में हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000075110","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Emergency & Constitutional Amendment","question":{"en":"Which constitutional amendment introduced the Goods and Services Tax (GST) in India? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत में वस्तु एवं सेवा कर (GST) किस संविधान संशोधन द्वारा लागू किया गया? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"97<sup>th</sup> Amendment","hi":"97वाँ संशोधन"},"2":{"en":"99<sup>th</sup> Amendment","hi":"99वाँ संशोधन"},"3":{"en":"101<sup>st</sup> Amendment","hi":"101वाँ संशोधन"},"4":{"en":"102<sup>nd</sup> Amendment","hi":"102वाँ संशोधन"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 101st Amendment</b><br>The <b>101st Constitutional Amendment Act, 2016</b> introduced the Goods and Services Tax by inserting <b>Articles 246A, 269A and 279A</b> and creating the GST Council.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• GST came into force on <b>1 July 2017</b> and replaced a large number of central and state indirect taxes with 'one nation, one tax'.<br>• <b>Article 279A</b> created the <b>GST Council</b>, chaired by the Union Finance Minister with state finance ministers as members.<br>• The <b>97th Amendment (2011)</b> related to cooperative societies, the <b>99th (2014)</b> to the National Judicial Appointments Commission and the <b>102nd (2018)</b> to constitutional status for the NCBC.<br>• GST is a destination-based tax on consumption with slabs of 5%, 12%, 18% and 28%.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because GST was introduced by the 101st Amendment.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 101वाँ संशोधन</b><br><b>101वें संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 2016</b> ने <b>अनुच्छेद 246A, 269A तथा 279A</b> जोड़कर वस्तु एवं सेवा कर लागू किया और जीएसटी परिषद का गठन किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• जीएसटी <b>1 जुलाई 2017</b> से प्रभावी हुआ और इसने अनेक केंद्रीय एवं राज्य अप्रत्यक्ष करों के स्थान पर 'एक राष्ट्र, एक कर' लागू किया।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 279A</b> ने <b>जीएसटी परिषद</b> बनाई, जिसके अध्यक्ष केंद्रीय वित्त मंत्री तथा सदस्य राज्यों के वित्त मंत्री होते हैं।<br>• <b>97वाँ संशोधन (2011)</b> सहकारी समितियों से, <b>99वाँ (2014)</b> राष्ट्रीय न्यायिक नियुक्ति आयोग से तथा <b>102वाँ (2018)</b> NCBC को संवैधानिक दर्जा देने से संबंधित था।<br>• जीएसटी उपभोग पर आधारित गंतव्य-आधारित कर है, जिसकी दरें 5%, 12%, 18% तथा 28% हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि जीएसटी 101वें संशोधन से लागू हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000075111","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Minerals","question":{"en":"Which state in India has one of the richest monazite deposits? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत के किस राज्य में मोनाज़ाइट के सर्वाधिक समृद्ध भंडारों में से एक है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Gujarat","hi":"गुजरात"},"2":{"en":"Rajasthan","hi":"राजस्थान"},"3":{"en":"Kerala","hi":"केरल"},"4":{"en":"Karnataka","hi":"कर्नाटक"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Kerala</b><br><b>Kerala</b> has one of the richest <b>monazite</b> deposits in India, found in the beach sands of the state, especially along the coast of <b>Kollam, Alappuzha and Thiruvananthapuram</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Monazite is the chief ore of <b>thorium</b> and also contains rare earth elements, and it is part of the 'placer' mineral sands found along the Kerala coast.<br>• India has among the world's largest thorium reserves, and the <b>Indian Rare Earths Limited</b> separates monazite at Manavalakurichi and Chavara.<br>• <b>Ilmenite, rutile, zircon and garnet</b> are the other heavy minerals mined from Kerala's beach sands.<br>• Because monazite is radioactive, its handling is regulated by the <b>Atomic Energy Act</b> and the Department of Atomic Energy.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because Kerala has one of India's richest monazite deposits.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – केरल</b><br>भारत में <b>मोनाज़ाइट (Monazite)</b> के सर्वाधिक समृद्ध भंडारों में से एक <b>केरल</b> में है, जो राज्य की समुद्री रेतों में, विशेषतः <b>कोल्लम, अलप्पुझा तथा तिरुवनंतपुरम</b> के तट पर पाया जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मोनाज़ाइट <b>थोरियम</b> का प्रमुख अयस्क है और इसमें दुर्लभ मृदा तत्व भी होते हैं; यह केरल तट की 'प्लेसर' खनिज रेतों का भाग है।<br>• भारत में विश्व के सबसे बड़े थोरियम भंडारों में से एक है, तथा <b>इंडियन रेयर अर्थ्स लिमिटेड</b> मनवालाकुरिची तथा चवरा में मोनाज़ाइट पृथक करता है।<br>• <b>इल्मेनाइट, रूटाइल, ज़र्कॉन तथा गार्नेट</b> केरल की समुद्री रेतों से निकाले जाने वाले अन्य भारी खनिज हैं।<br>• मोनाज़ाइट रेडियोधर्मी होने के कारण इसका प्रबंधन <b>परमाणु ऊर्जा अधिनियम</b> तथा परमाणु ऊर्जा विभाग द्वारा नियंत्रित होता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि भारत के सर्वाधिक समृद्ध मोनाज़ाइट भंडारों में से एक केरल में है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000075112","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"What medal did Neeraj Chopra win in the men's javelin throw event at the Paris 2024 Olympic Games? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"पेरिस 2024 ओलंपिक खेलों में पुरुषों की भाला फेंक स्पर्धा में नीरज चोपड़ा ने कौन-सा पदक जीता? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Gold","hi":"स्वर्ण"},"2":{"en":"Silver","hi":"रजत"},"3":{"en":"Bronze","hi":"कांस्य"},"4":{"en":"None of these","hi":"इनमें से कोई नहीं"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Silver</b><br>At the <b>Paris 2024 Olympics</b>, <b>Neeraj Chopra</b> won the <b>silver medal</b> in the men's javelin throw with a best effort of 89.45 m, finishing behind Arshad Nadeem of Pakistan.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Neeraj Chopra had won the <b>gold</b> at the Tokyo 2020 Olympics with a throw of 87.58 m, India's first athletics gold.<br>• He is the first Indian track-and-field athlete to win <b>two Olympic medals</b> and also won the World Championship title in 2023 (88.17 m).<br>• <b>Arshad Nadeem</b> set an Olympic record of 92.97 m in the Paris final.<br>• Manu Bhaker won two bronze medals in shooting at Paris 2024, taking India's total to six medals.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because Neeraj Chopra won silver at Paris 2024.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – रजत</b><br><b>पेरिस 2024 ओलंपिक</b> में <b>नीरज चोपड़ा</b> ने पुरुषों की भाला फेंक में 89.45 मीटर के सर्वश्रेष्ठ प्रयास के साथ <b>रजत पदक</b> जीता और पाकिस्तान के अरशद नदीम से पीछे रहे।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• नीरज चोपड़ा ने टोक्यो 2020 ओलंपिक में 87.58 मीटर के थ्रो के साथ <b>स्वर्ण</b> जीता था, जो भारत का एथलेटिक्स में पहला स्वर्ण था।<br>• वे <b>दो ओलंपिक पदक</b> जीतने वाले पहले भारतीय ट्रैक-एंड-फील्ड खिलाड़ी हैं तथा 2023 में विश्व चैंपियनशिप का खिताब (88.17 मीटर) भी जीता।<br>• <b>अरशद नदीम</b> ने पेरिस फाइनल में 92.97 मीटर का ओलंपिक रिकॉर्ड बनाया।<br>• पेरिस 2024 में मनु भाकर ने निशानेबाजी में दो कांस्य पदक जीते, जिससे भारत का कुल पदक छह हो गया।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि नीरज चोपड़ा ने पेरिस 2024 में रजत पदक जीता।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000075113","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"Which of the following cultural festivals are traditionally celebrated in Kerala? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-से सांस्कृतिक उत्सव पारंपरिक रूप से केरल में मनाए जाते हैं? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Guruvayur Ekadasi and Vasantholsavam","hi":"गुरुवायूर एकादशी तथा वसंतोल्सवम"},"2":{"en":"Karthigai Deepam and Chithirai Utsav","hi":"कार्तिगई दीपम तथा चिथिरई उत्सव"},"3":{"en":"Bhogali Bihu and Ambubachi Mahotsav","hi":"भोगाली बिहू तथा अंबुबाची महोत्सव"},"4":{"en":"Durga Puja and Jagannath Ratha Yatra","hi":"दुर्गा पूजा तथा जगन्नाथ रथ यात्रा"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Guruvayur Ekadasi and Vasantholsavam</b><br><b>Guruvayur Ekadasi</b> at the Guruvayur Sree Krishna temple and <b>Vasantholsavam</b> (the temple spring festival) are celebrated in <b>Kerala</b>, along with Onam, Vishu and Thrissur Pooram.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Karthigai Deepam</b> and <b>Chithirai Utsav</b> are Tamil festivals, celebrated mainly in Tamil Nadu.<br>• <b>Bhogali Bihu</b> and <b>Ambubachi Mahotsav</b> belong to <b>Assam</b>, the latter at the Kamakhya temple.<br>• <b>Durga Puja</b> is the biggest festival of West Bengal and the <b>Jagannath Rath Yatra</b> belongs to Puri in Odisha.<br>• Kerala's own major festivals include <b>Onam, Vishu, Thrissur Pooram, Attukal Pongala and Sabarimala Makaravilakku</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because both Guruvayur Ekadasi and Vasantholsavam are Kerala festivals.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – गुरुवायूर एकादशी तथा वसंतोल्सवम</b><br>गुरुवायूर श्रीकृष्ण मंदिर की <b>गुरुवायूर एकादशी</b> तथा <b>वसंतोल्सवम</b> (मंदिर का वसंत उत्सव) <b>केरल</b> में मनाए जाते हैं, साथ ही ओणम, विशु तथा त्रिशूर पूरम भी।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>कार्तिगई दीपम</b> तथा <b>चिथिरई उत्सव</b> तमिल उत्सव हैं, जो मुख्यतः तमिलनाडु में मनाए जाते हैं।<br>• <b>भोगाली बिहू</b> तथा <b>अंबुबाची महोत्सव</b> <b>असम</b> के उत्सव हैं, जिनमें से दूसरा कामाख्या मंदिर में होता है।<br>• <b>दुर्गा पूजा</b> पश्चिम बंगाल का सबसे बड़ा उत्सव है तथा <b>जगन्नाथ रथ यात्रा</b> ओडिशा के पुरी का उत्सव है।<br>• केरल के अपने प्रमुख उत्सवों में <b>ओणम, विशु, त्रिशूर पूरम, अट्टुकाल पोंगाला तथा सबरीमाला मकरविलक्कु</b> सम्मिलित हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि गुरुवायूर एकादशी तथा वसंतोल्सवम दोनों केरल के उत्सव हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000075114","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"In Badminton, which term describes a soft shot hit just over the net, forcing the opponent to move forward? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"बैडमिंटन में किस शब्द का प्रयोग उस कोमल शॉट के लिए होता है जो नेट के बिल्कुल ऊपर से जाकर प्रतिद्वंद्वी को आगे बढ़ने पर विवश करता है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Smash","hi":"स्मैश"},"2":{"en":"Drive","hi":"ड्राइव"},"3":{"en":"Drop Shot","hi":"ड्रॉप शॉट"},"4":{"en":"Clear","hi":"क्लियर"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Drop Shot</b><br>A <b>drop shot</b> in badminton is a soft, delicately played shot that just clears the net and falls close to it, forcing the opponent to move forward to the forecourt.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• A <b>smash</b> is a fast, downward attacking shot, a <b>drive</b> is a flat hard shot and a <b>clear</b> is a high defensive shot to the back court.<br>• The drop shot is most effective when it is disguised as a smash, so the opponent moves backward while the shuttle falls short.<br>• Badminton is played to <b>21 points</b> per game, best of three, with a change of ends every 11 points in the decider.<br>• The <b>BWF World Championships</b> and Thomas Cup (men) and Uber Cup (women) are its major team and individual events.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because the described soft net shot is the drop shot.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – ड्रॉप शॉट</b><br>बैडमिंटन में <b>ड्रॉप शॉट (Drop Shot)</b> एक कोमल, सूक्ष्म शॉट है जो नेट के ठीक ऊपर से जाकर उसके निकट गिरता है और प्रतिद्वंद्वी को आगे फोरकोर्ट तक आने पर विवश करता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>स्मैश</b> तेज नीचे की ओर आक्रामक शॉट है, <b>ड्राइव</b> सपाट तेज शॉट तथा <b>क्लियर</b> पिछले कोर्ट तक का ऊँचा बचाव शॉट है।<br>• ड्रॉप शॉट तब सर्वाधिक प्रभावी होता है जब इसे स्मैश के भ्रम में खेला जाए, जिससे प्रतिद्वंद्वी पीछे जाए और शटल आगे गिरे।<br>• बैडमिंटन <b>21 अंकों</b> के गेम में तीन में से दो जीतने के आधार पर खेला जाता है, तथा निर्णायक गेम में 11 अंक पर कोर्ट बदला जाता है।<br>• <b>BWF विश्व चैंपियनशिप</b> तथा थॉमस कप (पुरुष) एवं ऊबर कप (महिला) इसके प्रमुख आयोजन हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि वर्णित कोमल नेट शॉट ड्रॉप शॉट है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000075115","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Vedic Age","question":{"en":"What archaeological evidence from the Swat Valley points to the arrival of Aryan herdsmen around 1400 BC? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"स्वात घाटी से प्राप्त कौन-सा पुरातात्विक प्रमाण लगभग 1400 ईसा पूर्व में आर्य पशुपालकों के आगमन की ओर संकेत करता है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Pre-Aryan proto-urban ruins","hi":"आर्य-पूर्व प्रोटो-शहरी अवशेष"},"2":{"en":"Decorative swastika temple walls","hi":"सजावटी स्वस्तिक युक्त मंदिर दीवारें"},"3":{"en":"Advanced iron smelting furnaces","hi":"उन्नत लोहा गलाने की भट्टियाँ"},"4":{"en":"Horse remains and burials","hi":"अश्व अवशेष तथा समाधियाँ"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Horse remains and burials</b><br>The <b>horse remains and horse burials</b> found in the Swat Valley (Gandhara region) are dated to about <b>1400 BCE</b> and are taken as evidence of the arrival of Indo-Aryan speaking herdsmen who used the horse.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Swat Valley sites were excavated by the Italian Archaeological Mission, and the horse burials there are compared with the <b>Gandhara Grave Culture</b>.<br>• The horse was central to the Vedic people, who used it for chariot warfare, as seen in the <b>Rig Veda</b> descriptions of Ashwins and the horse sacrifice.<br>• <b>Painted Grey Ware</b> and iron tools belong to the later Vedic period, not to this phase.<br>• Swastika motifs appear mainly in painted pottery, not as temple walls, and pre-Aryan proto-urban ruins belong to the Harappan period.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because horse remains and burials tie the Swat Valley to Aryan herdsmen.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – अश्व अवशेष तथा समाधियाँ</b><br>स्वात घाटी (गांधार क्षेत्र) में पाए गए <b>अश्व अवशेष तथा अश्व-समाधियाँ</b> लगभग <b>1400 ईसा पूर्व</b> की हैं और इन्हें अश्व का उपयोग करने वाले इंडो-आर्य भाषी पशुपालकों के आगमन का प्रमाण माना जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• स्वात घाटी के स्थलों की खुदाई इतालवी पुरातात्विक मिशन ने की, और वहाँ की अश्व-समाधियों की तुलना <b>गांधार समाधि संस्कृति</b> से की जाती है।<br>• अश्व वैदिक लोगों के केंद्र में था, जो उसका उपयोग रथ युद्ध में करते थे, जैसा <b>ऋग्वेद</b> के अश्विन तथा अश्वमेध वर्णनों से दिखता है।<br>• <b>चित्रित धूसर मृदभांड (Painted Grey Ware)</b> तथा लोहे के औज़ार उत्तरवैदिक काल के हैं, इस चरण के नहीं।<br>• स्वस्तिक अलंकरण मुख्यतः चित्रित मृदभांडों पर मिलता है, मंदिर दीवारों पर नहीं, तथा आर्य-पूर्व प्रोटो-शहरी अवशेष हड़प्पा काल के हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि अश्व अवशेष तथा समाधियाँ स्वात घाटी को आर्य पशुपालकों से जोड़ती हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000075116","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Justice V. Ramasubramanian, who assumed office in late 2024, heads which statutory body responsible for safeguarding civil liberties in 2026? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"न्यायमूर्ति वी. रामसुब्रमण्यम, जिन्होंने 2024 के अंत में पदभार ग्रहण किया, 2026 में नागरिक स्वतंत्रताओं की रक्षा हेतु उत्तरदायी किस सांविधिक निकाय के प्रमुख हैं? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"National Commission for Scheduled Castes","hi":"राष्ट्रीय अनुसूचित जाति आयोग"},"2":{"en":"National Human Rights Commission","hi":"राष्ट्रीय मानवाधिकार आयोग"},"3":{"en":"National Commission for Minorities","hi":"राष्ट्रीय अल्पसंख्यक आयोग"},"4":{"en":"Law Commission of India","hi":"भारत विधि आयोग"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – National Human Rights Commission</b><br><b>Justice V. Ramasubramanian</b>, a former judge of the Supreme Court, took charge as the <b>Chairperson of the National Human Rights Commission (NHRC)</b> in December 2024 and heads the statutory body that safeguards civil liberties.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The NHRC was set up under the <b>Protection of Human Rights Act, 1993</b>, and is a statutory, not a constitutional, body.<br>• The NHRC Chairperson is appointed by the <b>President</b> on the recommendation of a committee headed by the Prime Minister.<br>• The Commission has the powers of a <b>civil court</b> during inquiries, but it cannot enforce its own orders.<br>• The <b>National Commission for Scheduled Castes</b> and the <b>National Commission for Minorities</b> are separate bodies, and the <b>Law Commission</b> is an executive advisory body.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because Justice Ramasubramanian heads the NHRC.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – राष्ट्रीय मानवाधिकार आयोग</b><br>सर्वोच्च न्यायालय के पूर्व न्यायाधीश <b>न्यायमूर्ति वी. रामसुब्रमण्यम (Justice V. Ramasubramanian)</b> ने दिसंबर 2024 में <b>राष्ट्रीय मानवाधिकार आयोग (NHRC) के अध्यक्ष</b> का पदभार ग्रहण किया और वे नागरिक स्वतंत्रताओं की रक्षा करने वाले इस सांविधिक निकाय के प्रमुख हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• NHRC की स्थापना <b>मानव अधिकार संरक्षण अधिनियम, 1993</b> के अंतर्गत हुई और यह सांविधिक (संवैधानिक नहीं) निकाय है।<br>• NHRC अध्यक्ष की नियुक्ति <b>राष्ट्रपति</b> द्वारा प्रधानमंत्री की अध्यक्षता वाली समिति की सिफारिश पर होती है।<br>• जाँच के समय आयोग को <b>सिविल न्यायालय</b> की शक्तियाँ प्राप्त होती हैं, परंतु वह अपने आदेशों को प्रवर्तित नहीं कर सकता।<br>• <b>राष्ट्रीय अनुसूचित जाति आयोग</b> तथा <b>राष्ट्रीय अल्पसंख्यक आयोग</b> पृथक निकाय हैं, और <b>विधि आयोग</b> कार्यकारी सलाहकार निकाय है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि न्यायमूर्ति रामसुब्रमण्यम NHRC के प्रमुख हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000075117","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"General Anil Chauhan, whose tenure was extended in late 2025, serves as the principal military advisor to the Government of India in which role? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"जनरल अनिल चौहान, जिनका कार्यकाल 2025 के अंत में बढ़ाया गया, भारत सरकार के प्रधान सैन्य सलाहकार के रूप में किस भूमिका में हैं? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Chief of the Army Staff","hi":"थलसेना स्टाफ प्रमुख"},"2":{"en":"Chief of Defence Staff","hi":"चीफ ऑफ डिफेंस स्टाफ"},"3":{"en":"National Security Advisor","hi":"राष्ट्रीय सुरक्षा सलाहकार"},"4":{"en":"Secretary, Ministry of Defence","hi":"रक्षा मंत्रालय के सचिव"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Chief of Defence Staff</b><br><b>General Anil Chauhan</b> is the <b>Chief of Defence Staff (CDS)</b>, the principal military adviser to the Government of India and the head of the Department of Military Affairs, and his tenure was extended in late 2025.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The post of CDS was created in <b>2019</b> on the recommendation of the Kargil Review Committee and the Shekatkar Committee; <b>General Bipin Rawat</b> was India's first CDS.<br>• The CDS heads the <b>Department of Military Affairs</b> in the Ministry of Defence and is a four-star officer with a fixed tenure extension provision.<br>• <b>General Upendra Dwivedi</b> is the Chief of the Army Staff, and the National Security Adviser is <b>Ajit Doval</b>.<br>• The CDS is a member of the <b>Defence Planning Committee</b> and the Nuclear Command Authority's Political Council.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because General Anil Chauhan serves as Chief of Defence Staff.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – चीफ ऑफ डिफेंस स्टाफ</b><br><b>जनरल अनिल चौहान (General Anil Chauhan)</b> <b>चीफ ऑफ डिफेंस स्टाफ (CDS)</b> हैं, जो भारत सरकार के प्रधान सैन्य सलाहकार तथा सैन्य मामलों के विभाग के प्रमुख हैं, और 2025 के अंत में उनका कार्यकाल बढ़ाया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• CDS का पद <b>2019</b> में कारगिल समीक्षा समिति तथा शेकटकर समिति की सिफारिश पर बनाया गया; <b>जनरल बिपिन रावत</b> भारत के प्रथम CDS थे।<br>• CDS रक्षा मंत्रालय के <b>सैन्य मामलों के विभाग</b> के प्रमुख हैं तथा चार-सितारा अधिकारी हैं, जिनके कार्यकाल विस्तार का प्रावधान है।<br>• <b>जनरल उपेंद्र द्विवेदी</b> थलसेना स्टाफ प्रमुख हैं, तथा राष्ट्रीय सुरक्षा सलाहकार <b>अजीत डोभाल</b> हैं।<br>• CDS <b>रक्षा योजना समिति</b> तथा परमाणु कमान प्राधिकरण की राजनीतिक परिषद के सदस्य हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि जनरल अनिल चौहान चीफ ऑफ डिफेंस स्टाफ हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000075118","section":"GK","topic":"Science and Technology: Science and Technology","question":{"en":"Which module of the Sanchar Saathi portal enables citizens to block their lost or stolen mobile phones across India? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"संचार साथी पोर्टल का कौन-सा मॉड्यूल नागरिकों को पूरे भारत में अपने खोए या चोरी हुए मोबाइल फोन ब्लॉक करने की सुविधा देता है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"TAFCOP (Telecom Analytics for Fraud Management and Consumer Protection)","hi":"TAFCOP (दूरसंचार विश्लेषण, धोखाधड़ी प्रबंधन तथा उपभोक्ता संरक्षण)"},"2":{"en":"CEIR (Central Equipment Identity Register)","hi":"CEIR (केंद्रीय उपकरण पहचान पंजिका)"},"3":{"en":"RICWIN (Report Incoming International Call With Indian Number)","hi":"RICWIN (भारतीय नंबर के साथ आने वाली अंतर्राष्ट्रीय कॉल का विनियमन)"},"4":{"en":"KYM (Know Your Mobile)","hi":"KYM (अपने मोबाइल को जानें)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – CEIR (Central Equipment Identity Register)</b><br>The <b>CEIR</b> module of the Sanchar Saathi portal lets a citizen <b>block a lost or stolen mobile phone</b> across all networks in India and later unblock it using the IMEI number.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Sanchar Saathi</b> was launched by the Department of Telecommunications in 2023 and has modules such as <b>CEIR, TAFCOP, Know Your Mobile, Chakshu</b> and the Digital Intelligence Platform.<br>• Blocking works on the <b>IMEI</b> of the handset, so the same SIM in a different phone will still function.<br>• <b>TAFCOP</b> lets a user check how many mobile connections are registered in their name, and <b>Chakshu</b> is used to report suspected fraud communications.<br>• <b>KYM (Know Your Mobile)</b> lets users verify the genuineness of a handset before buying it.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because CEIR is the module for blocking lost or stolen phones.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – CEIR (केंद्रीय उपकरण पहचान पंजिका)</b><br>संचार साथी पोर्टल का <b>CEIR</b> मॉड्यूल नागरिक को भारत के सभी नेटवर्कों पर <b>खोए या चोरी हुए मोबाइल फोन को ब्लॉक</b> करने तथा बाद में IMEI संख्या का उपयोग करके अनब्लॉक करने की सुविधा देता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>संचार साथी</b> को दूरसंचार विभाग ने 2023 में शुरू किया, जिसके <b>CEIR, TAFCOP, Know Your Mobile, चक्षु</b> तथा डिजिटल इंटेलिजेंस प्लेटफॉर्म जैसे मॉड्यूल हैं।<br>• ब्लॉकिंग हैंडसेट के <b>IMEI</b> पर होती है, इसलिए दूसरे फोन में वही सिम कार्य करती रहेगी।<br>• <b>TAFCOP</b> से उपयोगकर्ता अपने नाम पर पंजीकृत मोबाइल कनेक्शन देख सकता है, तथा <b>चक्षु</b> से संदिग्ध धोखाधड़ी वाले संचार की शिकायत की जाती है।<br>• <b>KYM (अपने मोबाइल को जानें)</b> से उपयोगकर्ता खरीदने से पहले हैंडसेट की प्रामाणिकता जाँच सकता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि खोए या चोरी हुए फोन को ब्लॉक करने का मॉड्यूल CEIR है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000075119","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"In India, under which health scheme are healthcare benefits provided to gig and platform workers as announced in the Union Budget 2025-26? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत में केंद्रीय बजट 2025-26 में घोषित अनुसार, गिग तथा प्लेटफॉर्म श्रमिकों को किस स्वास्थ्य योजना के अंतर्गत स्वास्थ्य लाभ प्रदान किए जाते हैं? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"NUHM (National Urban Health Mission)","hi":"NUHM (राष्ट्रीय शहरी स्वास्थ्य मिशन)"},"2":{"en":"AB-PMJAY (Ayushman Bharat Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana)","hi":"AB-PMJAY (आयुष्मान भारत प्रधानमंत्री जन आरोग्य योजना)"},"3":{"en":"PM-KUSUM (Pradhan Mantri Kisan Urja Suraksha evam Utthan Mahabhiyan)","hi":"PM-KUSUM (प्रधानमंत्री किसान ऊर्जा सुरक्षा एवं उत्थान महाभियान)"},"4":{"en":"Mission Indradhanush","hi":"मिशन इंद्रधनुष"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – AB-PMJAY (Ayushman Bharat Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana)</b><br>In the <b>Union Budget 2025-26</b> the government announced that <b>gig and platform workers</b> will be provided healthcare benefits under <b>AB-PMJAY</b>, extending the scheme's cover to this new category of workers.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• AB-PMJAY was launched in <b>2018</b> and gives health cover of <b>₹5 lakh per family per year</b> for secondary and tertiary hospitalisation.<br>• It is run by the <b>National Health Authority</b> and uses the Ayushman card for cashless treatment at empanelled hospitals.<br>• The <b>Code on Social Security, 2020</b> recognises gig workers and platform workers as a separate category and provides for their welfare, including a Social Security Fund.<br>• <b>NUHM</b> is a component of the National Health Mission, and <b>PM-KUSUM</b> and <b>Mission Indradhanush</b> relate to solar pumps and immunisation respectively.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because gig and platform workers are covered under AB-PMJAY.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – AB-PMJAY (आयुष्मान भारत प्रधानमंत्री जन आरोग्य योजना)</b><br><b>केंद्रीय बजट 2025-26</b> में घोषित किया गया कि <b>गिग तथा प्लेटफॉर्म श्रमिकों</b> को <b>AB-PMJAY</b> के अंतर्गत स्वास्थ्य लाभ दिए जाएँगे, जिससे योजना का दायरा श्रमिकों की इस नई श्रेणी तक बढ़ेगा।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• AB-PMJAY 2018 में शुरू हुई और द्वितीयक एवं तृतीयक अस्पताल में भर्ती के लिए <b>प्रति परिवार प्रति वर्ष ₹5 लाख</b> का स्वास्थ्य कवर देती है।<br>• इसे <b>राष्ट्रीय स्वास्थ्य प्राधिकरण</b> संचालित करता है और सूचीबद्ध अस्पतालों में कैशलेस उपचार के लिए आयुष्मान कार्ड का उपयोग होता है।<br>• <b>सामाजिक सुरक्षा संहिता, 2020</b> गिग श्रमिकों तथा प्लेटफॉर्म श्रमिकों को पृथक श्रेणी के रूप में मान्यता देती है और सामाजिक सुरक्षा कोष सहित उनके कल्याण का प्रावधान करती है।<br>• <b>NUHM</b> राष्ट्रीय स्वास्थ्य मिशन का घटक है, तथा <b>PM-KUSUM</b> एवं <b>मिशन इंद्रधनुष</b> क्रमशः सौर पंपों तथा टीकाकरण से संबंधित हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि गिग तथा प्लेटफॉर्म श्रमिक AB-PMJAY के अंतर्गत आते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000075120","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: International News","question":{"en":"Which of the following concepts is most closely associated with the geopolitical aspirations of BRICS (Brazil, Russia, India, China, and South Africa)? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी अवधारणा ब्रिक्स (ब्राज़ील, रूस, भारत, चीन तथा दक्षिण अफ्रीका) की भू-राजनीतिक आकांक्षाओं से सर्वाधिक निकटता से जुड़ी है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Liberal interventionism","hi":"उदार हस्तक्षेपवाद"},"2":{"en":"Mercantilist isolationism","hi":"व्यापारिक अलगाववाद"},"3":{"en":"Strategic autonomy","hi":"रणनीतिक स्वायत्तता"},"4":{"en":"Democratic centralism","hi":"लोकतांत्रिक केंद्रीकरण"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Strategic autonomy</b><br><b>Strategic autonomy</b> – the ability to take independent foreign policy decisions without aligning with any single bloc – is the idea most closely linked with BRICS, which seeks a multipolar world and reform of global institutions.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• BRICS was formed in 2009 (BRIC) and South Africa joined in <b>2010</b>; the group expanded in 2024 with Egypt, Ethiopia, Iran, Saudi Arabia and the UAE.<br>• The group works through the <b>New Development Bank (NDB)</b> at Shanghai and the <b>Contingent Reserve Arrangement</b>.<br>• India's own foreign policy doctrine of <b>strategic autonomy</b> explains its participation in both BRICS and the Quad.<br>• <b>Liberal interventionism, mercantilist isolationism and democratic centralism</b> describe other, unrelated positions.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because strategic autonomy is the concept closest to BRICS' geopolitical aims.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – रणनीतिक स्वायत्तता</b><br><b>रणनीतिक स्वायत्तता (Strategic autonomy)</b> – किसी एक गुट के साथ संरेखित हुए बिना स्वतंत्र विदेश नीति निर्णय लेने की क्षमता – ब्रिक्स से सर्वाधिक निकटता से जुड़ी अवधारणा है, क्योंकि यह समूह बहुध्रुवीय विश्व तथा वैश्विक संस्थानों में सुधार चाहता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ब्रिक्स 2009 (BRIC) में बना और दक्षिण अफ्रीका <b>2010</b> में जुड़ा; 2024 में मिस्र, इथियोपिया, ईरान, सऊदी अरब तथा UAE के साथ समूह का विस्तार हुआ।<br>• यह समूह शंघाई स्थित <b>न्यू डेवलपमेंट बैंक (NDB)</b> तथा <b>आकस्मिक आरक्षित व्यवस्था (CRA)</b> के माध्यम से कार्य करता है।<br>• भारत की <b>रणनीतिक स्वायत्तता</b> की विदेश नीति अवधारणा ब्रिक्स तथा क्वाड दोनों में उसकी भागीदारी की व्याख्या करती है।<br>• <b>उदार हस्तक्षेपवाद, व्यापारिक अलगाववाद तथा लोकतांत्रिक केंद्रीकरण</b> अन्य, असंबंधित दृष्टिकोणों का वर्णन करते हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि रणनीतिक स्वायत्तता ब्रिक्स के भू-राजनीतिक लक्ष्यों के सर्वाधिक निकट है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000075121","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"A and B jointly decide to starve prisoner Z to death. A withholds food during the first three days, and B continues the omission during the next three days, causing Z's death. Under Section 3(8) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 in India, which of the following best describes their liability? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"A तथा B मिलकर बंदी Z को भूखा रखकर मारने का निश्चय करते हैं। A पहले तीन दिन भोजन नहीं देता और B अगले तीन दिन यह चूक जारी रखता है, जिससे Z की मृत्यु हो जाती है। भारत में भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023 की धारा 3(8) के अंतर्गत उनका दायित्व सर्वोत्तम रूप से किस प्रकार वर्णित है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only B is guilty because his omission directly caused death.","hi":"केवल B दोषी है क्योंकि उसकी चूक से सीधे मृत्यु हुई।"},"2":{"en":"Only A is guilty because he initiated the act.","hi":"केवल A दोषी है क्योंकि उसने कार्य आरंभ किया।"},"3":{"en":"Both A and B are guilty of murder through intentional cooperation.","hi":"A तथा B दोनों जानबूझकर सहयोग के माध्यम से हत्या के दोषी हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Neither is guilty because omission alone cannot constitute murder.","hi":"कोई भी दोषी नहीं है क्योंकि केवल चूक से हत्या नहीं बनती।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Both A and B are guilty of murder through intentional cooperation.</b><br>Under Section 3(8) of the <b>Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023</b>, where several persons engage in a criminal act with a <b>common intention</b>, each of them is liable for the offence as if it were committed by him alone; here A and B shared the intention to kill Z and both carried out the act.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• This provision corresponds to Section 34 of the old Indian Penal Code and embodies the principle of <b>joint liability</b>.<br>• The act of starvation was done in <b>furtherance of the common intention</b>, so both are equally liable even if each performed only a part.<br>• Murder is punishable under <b>Section 103(1) of the BNS</b>, and a common intention can be formed just before the act.<br>• An omission can amount to an offence where there is a <b>legal duty</b> or a prior common design, so option (4) is wrong.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because both accused are guilty through intentional cooperation.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – A तथा B दोनों जानबूझकर सहयोग के माध्यम से हत्या के दोषी हैं।</b><br><b>भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023</b> की धारा 3(8) के अंतर्गत जहाँ कई व्यक्ति <b>सामान्य आशय</b> से आपराधिक कार्य करते हैं, वहाँ उनमें से प्रत्येक उस अपराध के लिए उसी प्रकार उत्तरदायी होता है मानो उसने अकेले ही किया हो; यहाँ A तथा B का Z को मारने का आशय समान था और दोनों ने कार्य किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह प्रावधान पुरानी भारतीय दंड संहिता की धारा 34 के समान है और <b>संयुक्त दायित्व</b> के सिद्धांत को मूर्त करता है।<br>• भूखा रखने का कार्य <b>सामान्य आशय की पूर्ति में</b> किया गया, इसलिए प्रत्येक के केवल भाग करने पर भी दोनों समान रूप से उत्तरदायी हैं।<br>• हत्या <b>BNS की धारा 103(1)</b> के अंतर्गत दंडनीय है, तथा सामान्य आशय कार्य से ठीक पहले भी बन सकता है।<br>• चूक भी अपराध हो सकती है जहाँ <b>विधिक कर्तव्य</b> या पूर्व सामान्य योजना हो, इसलिए विकल्प (4) गलत है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि दोनों अभियुक्त जानबूझकर सहयोग द्वारा दोषी हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000075122","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"A police inspector investigated a criminal case. Later, due to the non-availability of prosecutors, the district magistrate appoints the same inspector as assistant public prosecutor for that case. Which of the following is correct under the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 in India? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक पुलिस निरीक्षक ने किसी आपराधिक मामले की जाँच की। बाद में, अभियोजकों की अनुपलब्धता के कारण जिला मजिस्ट्रेट ने उसी निरीक्षक को उस मामले का सहायक लोक अभियोजक नियुक्त किया। भारत में भारतीय नागरिक सुरक्षा संहिता, 2023 के अंतर्गत निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा सही है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Valid: because an inspector satisfies the rank requirement.","hi":"वैध: क्योंकि निरीक्षक पद के स्तर की शर्त को पूरा करता है।"},"2":{"en":"Invalid: investigating officer cannot act as assistant public prosecutor in the same case.","hi":"अवैध: जाँच अधिकारी उसी मामले में सहायक लोक अभियोजक नहीं बन सकता।"},"3":{"en":"Invalid: if the accused consents.","hi":"अवैध: यदि अभियुक्त सहमति दे।"},"4":{"en":"Valid: because the appointment is temporary.","hi":"वैध: क्योंकि नियुक्ति अस्थायी है।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Invalid: investigating officer cannot act as assistant public prosecutor in the same case.</b><br>Under the <b>Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023</b>, an officer who has <b>investigated the case cannot be appointed as an assistant public prosecutor</b> to conduct the prosecution in that same case, because he would be both investigator and prosecutor.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The provision corresponds to the rule in the old CrPC that preserves the <b>separation of investigation and prosecution</b>, which is essential for a fair trial.<br>• A police officer can be appointed as assistant public prosecutor only in exceptional circumstances, and <b>never in a case he himself investigated</b>.<br>• The consent of the accused cannot cure a defect of this nature, and the temporary nature of the appointment makes no difference.<br>• This rule supports the constitutional guarantee of a <b>fair trial under Article 21</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because the appointment is invalid for the same case the officer investigated.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – अवैध: जाँच अधिकारी उसी मामले में सहायक लोक अभियोजक नहीं बन सकता।</b><br><b>भारतीय नागरिक सुरक्षा संहिता, 2023</b> के अंतर्गत जिस अधिकारी ने <b>मामले की जाँच की हो, उसे उसी मामले में अभियोजन चलाने के लिए सहायक लोक अभियोजक नियुक्त नहीं किया जा सकता</b>, क्योंकि तब वह एक ही समय में जाँचकर्ता और अभियोजक दोनों होगा।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह प्रावधान पुरानी दंड प्रक्रिया संहिता के उस नियम के समान है जो <b>जाँच तथा अभियोजन के पृथक्करण</b> को सुरक्षित रखता है, जो निष्पक्ष विचारण के लिए आवश्यक है।<br>• पुलिस अधिकारी को असाधारण परिस्थितियों में ही सहायक लोक अभियोजक नियुक्त किया जा सकता है, और <b>जिस मामले की स्वयं जाँच की हो उसमें कभी नहीं</b>।<br>• अभियुक्त की सहमति इस प्रकार के दोष को दूर नहीं कर सकती, तथा नियुक्ति का अस्थायी होना कोई अंतर नहीं डालता।<br>• यह नियम <b>अनुच्छेद 21 के अंतर्गत निष्पक्ष विचारण</b> की संवैधानिक गारंटी को सहारा देता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि जिस मामले की स्वयं जाँच की गई उसी में नियुक्ति अवैध है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000075123","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Who was appointed as the Chief of the Air Staff (CAS) of the Indian Air Force in September 2024? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"सितंबर 2024 में भारतीय वायु सेना के वायुसेना स्टाफ प्रमुख (CAS) के रूप में किसे नियुक्त किया गया? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Air Chief Marshal V.R. Chaudhari","hi":"एयर चीफ मार्शल वी. आर. चौधरी"},"2":{"en":"Air Chief Marshal R.K.S. Bhadauria","hi":"एयर चीफ मार्शल आर. के. एस. भदौरिया"},"3":{"en":"Air Chief Marshal Amar Preet Singh","hi":"एयर चीफ मार्शल अमर प्रीत सिंह"},"4":{"en":"Air Chief Marshal B.S. Dhanoa","hi":"एयर चीफ मार्शल बी. एस. धनोआ"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Air Chief Marshal Amar Preet Singh</b><br><b>Air Chief Marshal Amar Preet Singh</b> took over as the <b>Chief of the Air Staff</b> on <b>30 September 2024</b>, succeeding Air Chief Marshal V.R. Chaudhari.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• He is the <b>28th Chief of the Air Staff</b> of India and is a fighter pilot who has flown the MiG-21, MiG-29 and Mirage 2000 aircraft.<br>• <b>Air Chief Marshal V.R. Chaudhari</b> was his predecessor (2021-2024); <b>R.K.S. Bhadauria</b> was CAS from 2019 to 2021 and <b>B.S. Dhanoa</b> from 2017 to 2019.<br>• The Chief of the Air Staff is the senior-most officer of the Indian Air Force and a member of the <b>Chiefs of Staff Committee</b>.<br>• The Indian Air Force was founded on <b>8 October 1932</b> and celebrates Air Force Day on that date.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because Air Chief Marshal Amar Preet Singh became CAS in September 2024.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – एयर चीफ मार्शल अमर प्रीत सिंह</b><br><b>एयर चीफ मार्शल अमर प्रीत सिंह (Air Chief Marshal Amar Preet Singh)</b> ने <b>30 सितंबर 2024</b> को एयर चीफ मार्शल वी. आर. चौधरी के स्थान पर <b>वायुसेना स्टाफ प्रमुख</b> का पदभार ग्रहण किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• वे भारत के <b>28वें वायुसेना स्टाफ प्रमुख</b> हैं और लड़ाकू पायलट हैं, जिन्होंने मिग-21, मिग-29 तथा मिराज 2000 उड़ाए हैं।<br>• <b>एयर चीफ मार्शल वी. आर. चौधरी</b> उनके पूर्ववर्ती (2021-2024) थे; <b>आर. के. एस. भदौरिया</b> 2019 से 2021 तथा <b>बी. एस. धनोआ</b> 2017 से 2019 तक प्रमुख रहे।<br>• वायुसेना स्टाफ प्रमुख भारतीय वायु सेना के वरिष्ठतम अधिकारी तथा <b>चीफ ऑफ स्टाफ कमेटी</b> के सदस्य होते हैं।<br>• भारतीय वायु सेना की स्थापना <b>8 अक्टूबर 1932</b> को हुई और उसी दिन वायु सेना दिवस मनाया जाता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि सितंबर 2024 में एयर चीफ मार्शल अमर प्रीत सिंह CAS बने।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000075124","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Basics of Environmental Sciences","question":{"en":"In June 2026, the discovery of a new genus and species of tiger moth named 'Antaram idukki' highlighted the rich but largely unexplored biodiversity of which mountain range? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"जून 2026 में 'अंतरम इडुक्की' नामक टाइगर मॉथ की नई वंश तथा प्रजाति की खोज ने किस पर्वत श्रेणी की समृद्ध परंतु अधिकांशतः अन्वेषित जैव विविधता को प्रकाशित किया? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Eastern Ghats","hi":"पूर्वी घाट"},"2":{"en":"Aravalli Range","hi":"अरावली श्रेणी"},"3":{"en":"Western Ghats","hi":"पश्चिमी घाट"},"4":{"en":"Vindhya Range","hi":"विंध्य श्रेणी"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Western Ghats</b><br>The new tiger moth genus and species <b>'Antaram idukki'</b>, reported in June 2026, was discovered in the <b>Western Ghats</b> and highlights the rich but largely unexplored insect biodiversity of this biodiversity hotspot.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Western Ghats are one of the world's <b>eight 'hottest' biodiversity hotspots</b> and a UNESCO World Heritage site, running along the west coast of India.<br>• Tiger moths belong to the family <b>Erebidae</b> and are known for their bright warning colouration and toxic defence chemicals.<br>• The Western Ghats harbour species such as the <b>lion-tailed macaque, Malabar hornbill and Nilgiri tahr</b>.<br>• The <b>Eastern Ghats, Aravalli and Vindhya</b> ranges are older and drier, with a different faunal composition.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because 'Antaram idukki' was discovered in the Western Ghats.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – पश्चिमी घाट</b><br>जून 2026 में प्रतिवेदित टाइगर मॉथ की नई वंश तथा प्रजाति <b>'अंतरम इडुक्की' (Antaram idukki)</b> <b>पश्चिमी घाट</b> में खोजी गई और यह इस जैव विविधता हॉटस्पॉट की समृद्ध परंतु अधिकांशतः अन्वेषित कीट जैव विविधता को प्रकाशित करती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पश्चिमी घाट विश्व के <b>आठ 'सर्वाधिक गर्म' जैव विविधता हॉटस्पॉट</b> में से एक तथा यूनेस्को विश्व धरोहर स्थल है, जो भारत के पश्चिमी तट के साथ फैला है।<br>• टाइगर मॉथ <b>Erebidae</b> कुल के हैं और अपने चमकीले चेतावनी रंग तथा विषैले रक्षात्मक रसायनों के लिए जाने जाते हैं।<br>• पश्चिमी घाट में <b>सिंहपुच्छ मकाक, मालाबार हॉर्नबिल तथा नीलगिरि तहर</b> जैसी प्रजातियाँ पाई जाती हैं।<br>• <b>पूर्वी घाट, अरावली तथा विंध्य</b> श्रेणियाँ अधिक प्राचीन और शुष्क हैं, जिनकी प्राणी-संरचना भिन्न है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि 'अंतरम इडुक्की' पश्चिमी घाट में खोजी गई।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000075125","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Which of the following is the strongest criticism of excessive reliance on market forces in India after the 1991 economic reforms? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"1991 के आर्थिक सुधारों के बाद भारत में बाजार शक्तियों पर अत्यधिक निर्भरता की सबसे प्रबल आलोचना निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Markets generally reduce productivity","hi":"बाजार सामान्यतः उत्पादकता घटाते हैं"},"2":{"en":"Markets may neglect marginalized groups without state support","hi":"बाजार राज्य के समर्थन के बिना हाशिये के समूहों की उपेक्षा कर सकते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Markets usually prevent innovation","hi":"बाजार सामान्यतः नवाचार रोकते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Markets always ensure equitable outcomes","hi":"बाजार सदैव समान परिणाम सुनिश्चित करते हैं"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Markets may neglect marginalized groups without state support</b><br>The strongest criticism is that <b>markets, left entirely to themselves, may neglect marginalized groups</b> – the poor, informal workers, tribal communities and remote regions – because they respond to purchasing power rather than need, so state support and public provisioning remain essential.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The 1991 reforms liberalised, privatised and globalised the economy, but their social impact required schemes such as <b>MGNREGA, the Food Security Act and Jan Aushadhi</b> to protect the poor.<br>• Market failure occurs in <b>public goods, merit goods, externalities and information asymmetry</b>, which is why the state regulates and provides.<br>• The other options are factually wrong, since markets are generally associated with <b>higher productivity and innovation</b>, and they do not guarantee equitable outcomes.<br>• Amartya Sen's capability approach argues for state action to build <b>human capabilities alongside markets</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because neglecting marginalized groups is the real criticism of market reliance.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – बाजार राज्य के समर्थन के बिना हाशिये के समूहों की उपेक्षा कर सकते हैं</b><br>सबसे प्रबल आलोचना यह है कि <b>पूर्णतः स्वतंत्र छोड़े गए बाजार हाशिये के समूहों</b> – गरीब, अनौपचारिक श्रमिक, आदिवासी समुदाय तथा दूरस्थ क्षेत्र – <b>की उपेक्षा कर सकते हैं</b>, क्योंकि वे आवश्यकता के स्थान पर क्रयशक्ति पर प्रतिक्रिया देते हैं; इसलिए राज्य का समर्थन तथा सार्वजनिक प्रावधान आवश्यक रहता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 1991 के सुधारों ने अर्थव्यवस्था का उदारीकरण, निजीकरण तथा वैश्वीकरण किया, परंतु उनके सामाजिक प्रभाव के लिए गरीबों की रक्षा हेतु <b>मनरेगा, खाद्य सुरक्षा अधिनियम तथा जन औषधि</b> जैसी योजनाएँ आवश्यक हुईं।<br>• बाजार विफलता <b>सार्वजनिक वस्तुओं, गुणवत्तापूर्ण वस्तुओं, बाह्यताओं तथा सूचना असममिति</b> में होती है, इसी कारण राज्य नियमन और प्रावधान करता है।<br>• अन्य विकल्प तथ्यात्मक रूप से गलत हैं, क्योंकि बाजार सामान्यतः <b>उच्च उत्पादकता एवं नवाचार</b> से जुड़े होते हैं और वे समान परिणाम की गारंटी नहीं देते।<br>• अमर्त्य सेन का क्षमता दृष्टिकोण बाजार के साथ-साथ <b>मानव क्षमताओं के निर्माण</b> हेतु राज्यीय कार्रवाई का पक्षधर है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि हाशिये के समूहों की उपेक्षा ही बाजार-निर्भरता की वास्तविक आलोचना है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000075126","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Reports and Indices","question":{"en":"The human development approach underlying the Human Development Index (HDI) is primarily concerned with which of the following? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"मानव विकास सूचकांक (HDI) के अंतर्गत मानव विकास दृष्टिकोण मुख्य रूप से निम्नलिखित में से किससे संबंधित है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Promotion of trade liberalization","hi":"व्यापार उदारीकरण को बढ़ावा देना"},"2":{"en":"Acceleration of urbanization","hi":"शहरीकरण को तेज करना"},"3":{"en":"Expansion of military power","hi":"सैन्य शक्ति का विस्तार"},"4":{"en":"Expansion of human capabilities","hi":"मानव क्षमताओं का विस्तार"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Expansion of human capabilities</b><br>The human development approach behind the HDI, developed by <b>Mahbub ul Haq and Amartya Sen</b>, is concerned with <b>expanding human capabilities</b> – living a long and healthy life, being educated and having a decent standard of living.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The capability approach sees development as <b>freedom and choice</b>, not merely growth of income.<br>• HDI measures three things – <b>life expectancy, years of schooling and GNI per capita</b> – and is published annually by UNDP.<br>• Trade liberalisation, urbanisation and military power are means or unrelated goals, not the purpose of human development.<br>• Related UNDP indices include the <b>Human Development Index, Inequality-adjusted HDI, Gender Development Index and Multidimensional Poverty Index</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because human development is about expanding human capabilities.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – मानव क्षमताओं का विस्तार</b><br>महबूब-उल-हक तथा अमर्त्य सेन द्वारा विकसित HDI के पीछे का मानव विकास दृष्टिकोण <b>मानव क्षमताओं के विस्तार</b> से संबंधित है – दीर्घ एवं स्वस्थ जीवन जीना, शिक्षित होना तथा सम्मानजनक जीवन-स्तर प्राप्त करना।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• क्षमता दृष्टिकोण विकास को केवल आय वृद्धि नहीं, बल्कि <b>स्वतंत्रता तथा विकल्प</b> मानता है।<br>• HDI तीन बातें मापता है – <b>जीवन प्रत्याशा, विद्यालयी वर्ष तथा प्रति व्यक्ति GNI</b> – और UNDP द्वारा प्रतिवर्ष प्रकाशित होता है।<br>• व्यापार उदारीकरण, शहरीकरण तथा सैन्य शक्ति साधन या असंबंधित लक्ष्य हैं, मानव विकास का उद्देश्य नहीं।<br>• UNDP के अन्य सूचकांकों में <b>मानव विकास सूचकांक, असमानता-समायोजित HDI, लैंगिक विकास सूचकांक तथा बहुआयामी गरीबी सूचकांक</b> सम्मिलित हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि मानव विकास का अर्थ मानव क्षमताओं का विस्तार है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000075127","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Ease of Doing Business reforms are most closely associated with which broader constitutional goal? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"व्यवसाय सुगमता (Ease of Doing Business) सुधार किस व्यापक संवैधानिक लक्ष्य से सर्वाधिक निकटता से जुड़े हैं? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Promoting judicial review and constitutional accountability","hi":"न्यायिक पुनरावलोकन तथा संवैधानिक उत्तरदायित्व को बढ़ावा देना"},"2":{"en":"Promoting emergency governance and constitutional stability","hi":"आपातकालीन शासन तथा संवैधानिक स्थिरता को बढ़ावा देना"},"3":{"en":"Promoting a welfare state and socioeconomic development","hi":"कल्याणकारी राज्य तथा सामाजिक-आर्थिक विकास को बढ़ावा देना"},"4":{"en":"Promoting electoral representation and constitutional participation","hi":"चुनावी प्रतिनिधित्व तथा संवैधानिक भागीदारी को बढ़ावा देना"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Promoting a welfare state and socioeconomic development</b><br>Ease of Doing Business reforms promote <b>enterprise, investment and jobs</b>, which serve the constitutional goal of a <b>welfare state and socioeconomic development</b> set out in the Directive Principles of State Policy.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Directive Principles in <b>Part IV (Articles 36-51)</b> direct the state to promote a social order in which justice – social, economic and political – informs national life.<br>• EoDB reforms include <b>single window clearance, online approvals, decriminalisation of minor offences, insolvency law and labour law simplification</b>.<br>• Judicial review, emergency provisions and electoral representation relate to other parts of the Constitution and are not the goal of business reform.<br>• India improved sharply in the World Bank's EoDB rankings before the index was discontinued in 2021, and now uses the <b>BRAP</b> framework.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because business reform ultimately serves the welfare state and socioeconomic development.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – कल्याणकारी राज्य तथा सामाजिक-आर्थिक विकास को बढ़ावा देना</b><br>व्यवसाय सुगमता सुधार <b>उद्यम, निवेश तथा रोजगार</b> को बढ़ावा देते हैं, जो राज्य के नीति निर्देशक तत्वों में उल्लिखित <b>कल्याणकारी राज्य तथा सामाजिक-आर्थिक विकास</b> के संवैधानिक लक्ष्य की पूर्ति करते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>भाग IV (अनुच्छेद 36-51)</b> के नीति निर्देशक तत्व राज्य को ऐसी सामाजिक व्यवस्था बनाने का निर्देश देते हैं जिसमें सामाजिक, आर्थिक तथा राजनीतिक न्याय राष्ट्रीय जीवन में व्याप्त हो।<br>• EoDB सुधारों में <b>एकल खिड़की मंजूरी, ऑनलाइन अनुमोदन, छोटे अपराधों का अपराधीकरण घटाना, दिवाला विधि तथा श्रम विधियों का सरलीकरण</b> सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• न्यायिक पुनरावलोकन, आपातकालीन प्रावधान तथा चुनावी प्रतिनिधित्व संविधान के अन्य भागों से संबंधित हैं और व्यवसाय सुधार का लक्ष्य नहीं हैं।<br>• विश्व बैंक के EoDB सूचकांक के 2021 में बंद होने से पहले भारत ने बड़ी प्रगति की थी, और अब <b>BRAP</b> रूपरेखा का उपयोग होता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि व्यवसाय सुधार अंततः कल्याणकारी राज्य तथा सामाजिक-आर्थिक विकास की सेवा करते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000075128","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Reports and Indices (Current)","question":{"en":"According to the World Happiness Report 2026, which of the following internet activities was associated with higher life satisfaction among 15-year-old students? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"विश्व प्रसन्नता प्रतिवेदन 2026 के अनुसार, निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी इंटरनेट गतिविधि 15 वर्षीय छात्रों में उच्च जीवन-संतुष्टि से जुड़ी थी? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Content creation","hi":"सामग्री सृजन (Content creation)"},"2":{"en":"Social media","hi":"सोशल मीडिया"},"3":{"en":"Browsing for fun","hi":"मनोरंजन के लिए ब्राउज़िंग"},"4":{"en":"Gaming","hi":"गेमिंग"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Content creation</b><br>According to the <b>World Happiness Report 2026</b>, <b>content creation</b> was the internet activity associated with <b>higher life satisfaction</b> among 15-year-old students, while passive and algorithm-driven use lowered wellbeing.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The 2026 report, the 14th edition, focused on <b>social media and youth well-being</b> and was published on 19 March 2026.<br>• It found that adolescents using social media for <b>less than one hour a day</b> reported the highest wellbeing, while heavy use, especially among girls, was linked to lower life satisfaction.<br>• <b>Active, creative use</b> of the internet (making and sharing content) had a positive association, unlike passive scrolling.<br>• The report is published by the Oxford Wellbeing Research Centre with Gallup and the UN SDSN, and ranks countries on the <b>Cantril Ladder</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because content creation was linked with higher life satisfaction.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – सामग्री सृजन (Content creation)</b><br><b>विश्व प्रसन्नता प्रतिवेदन 2026</b> के अनुसार 15 वर्षीय छात्रों में <b>सामग्री सृजन</b> वह इंटरनेट गतिविधि थी जो <b>उच्च जीवन-संतुष्टि</b> से जुड़ी थी, जबकि निष्क्रिय तथा एल्गोरिदम-चालित उपयोग कल्याण घटाता था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 2026 का प्रतिवेदन, जो 14वाँ संस्करण है, <b>सोशल मीडिया तथा युवा कल्याण</b> पर केंद्रित था और 19 मार्च 2026 को प्रकाशित हुआ।<br>• इसमें पाया गया कि <b>दिन में एक घंटे से कम</b> सोशल मीडिया उपयोग करने वाले किशोरों की भलाई सर्वाधिक थी, जबकि अत्यधिक उपयोग, विशेषतः लड़कियों में, कम जीवन-संतुष्टि से जुड़ा था।<br>• इंटरनेट का <b>सक्रिय, सृजनात्मक उपयोग</b> (सामग्री बनाना तथा साझा करना) सकारात्मक रूप से जुड़ा था, निष्क्रिय स्क्रॉलिंग के विपरीत।<br>• यह प्रतिवेदन ऑक्सफोर्ड वेलबीइंग रिसर्च सेंटर द्वारा गैलप तथा UN SDSN के साथ प्रकाशित होता है और देशों को <b>कैंट्रिल लैडर</b> पर रैंक करता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि सामग्री सृजन उच्च जीवन-संतुष्टि से जुड़ा था।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000075129","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Ecosystem","question":{"en":"Which of the following is a major cause of amphibian decline in India? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत में उभयचरों (Amphibians) के ह्रास का एक प्रमुख कारण निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Expansion of natural wetlands and suitable habitats","hi":"प्राकृतिक आर्द्रभूमियों तथा उपयुक्त आवासों का विस्तार"},"2":{"en":"Habitat loss, climate change and environmental pollution","hi":"आवास क्षति, जलवायु परिवर्तन तथा पर्यावरणीय प्रदूषण"},"3":{"en":"Increased breeding habitats and resource availability","hi":"प्रजनन आवासों तथा संसाधन उपलब्धता में वृद्धि"},"4":{"en":"Absence of invasive species and ecological competition","hi":"आक्रामक प्रजातियों तथा पारिस्थितिक प्रतिस्पर्धा का अभाव"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Habitat loss, climate change and environmental pollution</b><br>The major causes of amphibian decline in India are <b>habitat loss and fragmentation, climate change, pollution, pesticide run-off and disease</b>, along with invasive species.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Amphibians have <b>permeable skin</b> and biphasic life cycles, so they are highly sensitive to changes in water quality, temperature and moisture – they are excellent <b>bio-indicators</b>.<br>• The <b>Global Amphibian Assessment</b> lists a large share of amphibian species as threatened, making them the most threatened vertebrate class.<br>• <b>Chytridiomycosis</b>, caused by the fungus Batrachochytrium dendrobatidis, has caused declines worldwide.<br>• Expansion of wetlands, more breeding habitat and absence of invasive species would <b>help</b> amphibians, not harm them.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because habitat loss, climate change and pollution cause amphibian decline.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – आवास क्षति, जलवायु परिवर्तन तथा पर्यावरणीय प्रदूषण</b><br>भारत में उभयचरों के ह्रास के प्रमुख कारण <b>आवास क्षति एवं विखंडन, जलवायु परिवर्तन, प्रदूषण, कीटनाशकों का बहाव तथा रोग</b> हैं, साथ ही आक्रामक प्रजातियाँ भी।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• उभयचरों की <b>पारगम्य त्वचा</b> तथा द्वि-चरणीय जीवन चक्र होता है, इसलिए वे जल की गुणवत्ता, तापमान तथा नमी में परिवर्तन के प्रति अत्यधिक संवेदनशील हैं – वे उत्कृष्ट <b>जैव-संकेतक</b> हैं।<br>• <b>वैश्विक उभयचर आकलन</b> में उभयचर प्रजातियों का बड़ा भाग संकटग्रस्त है, जिससे ये सर्वाधिक संकटग्रस्त कशेरुकी वर्ग बन गए हैं।<br>• कवक Batrachochytrium dendrobatidis से होने वाला <b>काइट्रिडियोमाइकोसिस</b> विश्वभर में ह्रास का कारण बना है।<br>• आर्द्रभूमियों का विस्तार, प्रजनन आवास में वृद्धि तथा आक्रामक प्रजातियों का अभाव उभयचरों के लिए <b>लाभदायक</b> होंगे, हानिकारक नहीं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि आवास क्षति, जलवायु परिवर्तन तथा प्रदूषण उभयचर ह्रास के कारण हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000075130","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Ecosystem","question":{"en":"Which statement best describes the ecological importance of protozoa and zooplankton in aquatic ecosystems? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"जलीय पारिस्थितिकी तंत्रों में प्रोटोज़ोआ तथा जूप्लैंकटन के पारिस्थितिक महत्व का सर्वोत्तम वर्णन कौन-सा कथन करता है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"They are top carnivores in aquatic ecosystems.","hi":"वे जलीय पारिस्थितिकी तंत्रों के शीर्ष मांसाहारी हैं।"},"2":{"en":"They form the base of aquatic food chains.","hi":"वे जलीय खाद्य शृंखलाओं का आधार बनते हैं।"},"3":{"en":"They are responsible for coral bleaching.","hi":"वे प्रवाल विरंजन के लिए उत्तरदायी हैं।"},"4":{"en":"They only exist in marine ecosystems.","hi":"वे केवल समुद्री पारिस्थितिकी तंत्रों में पाए जाते हैं।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – They form the base of aquatic food chains.</b><br><b>Protozoa and zooplankton</b> are primary consumers that feed on phytoplankton and are themselves eaten by small fish, so they form the <b>base of aquatic food chains</b> and transfer energy up the food web.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Phytoplankton</b> are the producers of aquatic ecosystems, and zooplankton link them to fish – together they form the <b>pelagic food web</b>.<br>• Zooplankton include <b>copepods, krill, rotifers and cladocerans</b>; protozoa such as ciliates graze on bacteria and help in nutrient recycling.<br>• They are <b>not top carnivores</b>; top carnivores in aquatic systems are large fish, sharks and dolphins.<br>• Coral bleaching is caused by the loss of symbiotic <b>zooxanthellae</b> due to heat stress, not by zooplankton.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because protozoa and zooplankton form the base of aquatic food chains.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – वे जलीय खाद्य शृंखलाओं का आधार बनते हैं।</b><br><b>प्रोटोज़ोआ तथा जूप्लैंकटन</b> प्राथमिक उपभोक्ता हैं, जो फाइटोप्लैंकटन पर आहार लेते हैं और स्वयं छोटी मछलियों का आहार बनते हैं, इसलिए वे <b>जलीय खाद्य शृंखलाओं का आधार</b> बनाते हैं और ऊर्जा को खाद्य जाल में ऊपर स्थानांतरित करते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>फाइटोप्लैंकटन</b> जलीय पारिस्थितिकी तंत्र के उत्पादक हैं, और जूप्लैंकटन उन्हें मछलियों से जोड़ते हैं – दोनों मिलकर <b>पेलाजिक खाद्य जाल</b> बनाते हैं।<br>• जूप्लैंकटन में <b>कोपेपॉड, क्रिल, रोटिफर तथा क्लैडोसेरन</b> सम्मिलित हैं; सिलिएट जैसे प्रोटोज़ोआ जीवाणुओं पर आहार लेकर पोषक पुनर्चक्रण में सहायता करते हैं।<br>• वे <b>शीर्ष मांसाहारी नहीं</b> हैं; जलीय तंत्रों के शीर्ष मांसाहारी बड़ी मछलियाँ, शार्क तथा डॉल्फिन हैं।<br>• प्रवाल विरंजन ऊष्मा तनाव से सहजीवी <b>ज़ूजैंथेली</b> के नष्ट होने से होता है, जूप्लैंकटन से नहीं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि प्रोटोज़ोआ तथा जूप्लैंकटन जलीय खाद्य शृंखलाओं का आधार हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000075131","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"The value of \\(\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{8}\\) is: [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"\\(\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{8}\\) का मान है: [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rational","hi":"परिमेय"},"2":{"en":"Irrational","hi":"अपरिमेय"},"3":{"en":"Integer","hi":"पूर्णांक"},"4":{"en":"Whole number","hi":"पूर्ण संख्या"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{8} = \\sqrt{2} + 2\\sqrt{2} = 3\\sqrt{2}\\)<br>\\(3\\sqrt{2}\\) cannot be written as a ratio of two integers, so it is \\(\\boxed{\\text{Irrational}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Irrational.</b>","hi":"\\(\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{8} = \\sqrt{2} + 2\\sqrt{2} = 3\\sqrt{2}\\)<br>\\(3\\sqrt{2}\\) को दो पूर्णांकों के अनुपात में नहीं लिखा जा सकता, अतः यह \\(\\boxed{\\text{अपरिमेय}}\\) है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): अपरिमेय है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000075132","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"If the height of a regular right square pyramid is increased by 25% and the base side length is increased by 10%, by what percentage does the volume increase? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि एक समकोणीय वर्गीय पिरामिड की ऊँचाई 25% बढ़ा दी जाए और आधार की भुजा 10% बढ़ा दी जाए, तो आयतन कितने प्रतिशत बढ़ेगा? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"51.25%"},"2":{"en":"46.28%"},"3":{"en":"22.54%"},"4":{"en":"55.84%"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Volume \\(= \\frac{1}{3}a^2h\\). New side = \\(1.1a\\), new height = \\(1.25h\\)<br>New volume = \\(\\frac{1}{3}(1.1a)^2(1.25h) = 1.21 \\times 1.25 = 1.5125\\) times the old volume<br>Increase = \\((1.5125 - 1) \\times 100 = \\boxed{51.25\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 51.25%.</b>","hi":"आयतन \\(= \\frac{1}{3}a^2h\\); नई भुजा = \\(1.1a\\), नई ऊँचाई = \\(1.25h\\)<br>नया आयतन = \\(\\frac{1}{3}(1.1a)^2(1.25h) = 1.21 \\times 1.25 = 1.5125\\) गुना<br>वृद्धि = \\((1.5125 - 1) \\times 100 = \\boxed{51.25\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 51.25% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000075133","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Convert π/6 radians to degrees. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"π/6 रेडियन को डिग्री में बदलिए। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"60°"},"2":{"en":"45°"},"3":{"en":"30°"},"4":{"en":"90°"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\pi\\) radians = \\(180^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\frac{\\pi}{6} = \\frac{180^\\circ}{6} = \\boxed{30^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 30°.</b>","hi":"\\(\\pi\\) रेडियन = \\(180^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\frac{\\pi}{6} = \\frac{180^\\circ}{6} = \\boxed{30^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 30° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000075134","section":"MATH","topic":"Ratio and Proportion","question":{"en":"If A : B = 3 : 5 and A : C = 6 : 7, then B : C is: [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि A : B = 3 : 5 और A : C = 6 : 7 है, तो B : C है: [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"7:10"},"2":{"en":"5:7"},"3":{"en":"10:7"},"4":{"en":"7:5"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Make A the same in both ratios. LCM of 3 and 6 is 6.<br>A : B = \\(6 : 10\\), A : C = \\(6 : 7\\)<br>So B : C = \\(\\boxed{10 : 7}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 10:7.</b>","hi":"दोनों अनुपातों में A को समान कीजिए। 3 और 6 का ल.स. 6 है।<br>A : B = \\(6 : 10\\), A : C = \\(6 : 7\\)<br>अतः B : C = \\(\\boxed{10 : 7}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 10:7 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000075135","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"A sum of money doubles itself in 5 years at compound interest. Find the approximate rate of interest per annum. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज पर कोई धनराशि 5 वर्षों में दोगुनी हो जाती है। वार्षिक ब्याज दर लगभग ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"10.87%"},"2":{"en":"14.87%"},"3":{"en":"21.87%"},"4":{"en":"19.87%"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(2P = P\\left(1 + \\frac{r}{100}\\right)^5 \\Rightarrow \\left(1 + \\frac{r}{100}\\right) = 2^{1/5}\\)<br>\\(2^{1/5} = 1.1487\\)<br>\\(r = 14.87\\%\\) per annum, i.e. \\(\\boxed{14.87\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 14.87%.</b>","hi":"\\(2P = P\\left(1 + \\frac{r}{100}\\right)^5 \\Rightarrow \\left(1 + \\frac{r}{100}\\right) = 2^{1/5}\\)<br>\\(2^{1/5} = 1.1487\\)<br>\\(r = 14.87\\%\\) प्रति वर्ष, अर्थात् \\(\\boxed{14.87\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 14.87% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000075136","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"A tower is 90 m high. The angles of depression of two ships are 30° and 45°. Find the approximate distance between the ships. Use(√3=1.732) [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक मीनार 90 m ऊँची है। दो जहाज़ों के अवनमन कोण 30° और 45° हैं। जहाज़ों के बीच की अनुमानित दूरी ज्ञात कीजिए। (√3=1.732 लीजिए) [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"60 m"},"2":{"en":"56 m"},"3":{"en":"66 m"},"4":{"en":"62 m"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"For the far ship: \\(90\\cot 30^\\circ = 90\\sqrt{3} = 155.88\\) m<br>For the near ship: \\(90\\cot 45^\\circ = 90\\) m<br>Distance = \\(155.88 - 90 = 65.88 \\approx \\boxed{66}\\) m<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 66 m.</b>","hi":"दूर के जहाज़ के लिए: \\(90\\cot 30^\\circ = 90\\sqrt{3} = 155.88\\) m<br>निकट के जहाज़ के लिए: \\(90\\cot 45^\\circ = 90\\) m<br>दूरी = \\(155.88 - 90 = 65.88 \\approx \\boxed{66}\\) m<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 66 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000075137","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"A wire in the form of a circle of radius 21 cm is cut and bent into a rectangle whose sides are in the ratio 6 : 5. Find the area of the rectangle (Take π = 22/7). [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"21 cm त्रिज्या वाले वृत्त के रूप में एक तार को काटकर ऐसे आयत में मोड़ा जाता है जिसकी भुजाएँ 6 : 5 के अनुपात में हैं। आयत का क्षेत्रफल ज्ञात कीजिए (π = 22/7 लीजिए)। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1020 cm²"},"2":{"en":"1050 cm²"},"3":{"en":"1080 cm²"},"4":{"en":"1120 cm²"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Circumference of the circle = \\(2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 21 = 132\\) cm = perimeter of the rectangle<br>Let the sides be \\(6x\\) and \\(5x\\): \\(2(6x + 5x) = 132 \\Rightarrow 22x = 132 \\Rightarrow x = 6\\)<br>Sides = 36 cm and 30 cm<br>Area = \\(36 \\times 30 = \\boxed{1080}\\) cm²<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 1080 cm².</b>","hi":"वृत्त की परिधि = \\(2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 21 = 132\\) cm = आयत का परिमाप<br>भुजाएँ \\(6x\\) और \\(5x\\) मानिए: \\(2(6x + 5x) = 132 \\Rightarrow 22x = 132 \\Rightarrow x = 6\\)<br>भुजाएँ = 36 cm और 30 cm<br>क्षेत्रफल = \\(36 \\times 30 = \\boxed{1080}\\) cm²<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 1080 cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000075138","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If \\(\\cos\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta = 1\\), find the value of \\(\\sin^2\\theta + \\sin^4\\theta\\). [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि \\(\\cos\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta = 1\\) है, तो \\(\\sin^2\\theta + \\sin^4\\theta\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"1"},"4":{"en":"-1"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\cos\\theta = 1 - \\cos^2\\theta = \\sin^2\\theta\\)<br>\\(\\sin^2\\theta + \\sin^4\\theta = \\cos\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 1.</b>","hi":"\\(\\cos\\theta = 1 - \\cos^2\\theta = \\sin^2\\theta\\)<br>\\(\\sin^2\\theta + \\sin^4\\theta = \\cos\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000075139","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{12+q}+\\sqrt{12-q}}{\\sqrt{12+q}-\\sqrt{12-q}} = 3\\), then find the value of q. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{12+q}+\\sqrt{12-q}}{\\sqrt{12+q}-\\sqrt{12-q}} = 3\\) है, तो q का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{3}{4}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{36}{5}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{56}{9}\\)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Let \\(u = \\sqrt{12+q}\\), \\(v = \\sqrt{12-q}\\).<br>\\(\\frac{u+v}{u-v} = 3 \\Rightarrow u+v = 3u-3v \\Rightarrow \\frac{u}{v} = 2\\)<br>\\(\\frac{12+q}{12-q} = 4 \\Rightarrow 12 + q = 48 - 4q\\)<br>\\(5q = 36 \\Rightarrow q = \\boxed{\\frac{36}{5}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \\(\\frac{36}{5}\\).</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए \\(u = \\sqrt{12+q}\\), \\(v = \\sqrt{12-q}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{u+v}{u-v} = 3 \\Rightarrow u+v = 3u-3v \\Rightarrow \\frac{u}{v} = 2\\)<br>\\(\\frac{12+q}{12-q} = 4 \\Rightarrow 12 + q = 48 - 4q\\)<br>\\(5q = 36 \\Rightarrow q = \\boxed{\\frac{36}{5}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \\(\\frac{36}{5}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000075140","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"Find the value of \\(\\sqrt{17 - 2\\sqrt{72}} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17-2\\sqrt{72}}}\\). [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"\\(\\sqrt{17 - 2\\sqrt{72}} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17-2\\sqrt{72}}}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{2}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(-4\\sqrt{2}\\)"},"4":{"en":"1"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(2\\sqrt{72} = 12\\sqrt{2}\\), and \\((3 - 2\\sqrt{2})^2 = 17 - 12\\sqrt{2}\\)<br>So \\(\\sqrt{17 - 12\\sqrt{2}} = 3 - 2\\sqrt{2}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{3 - 2\\sqrt{2}} = 3 + 2\\sqrt{2}\\)<br>Expression = \\((3 - 2\\sqrt{2}) - (3 + 2\\sqrt{2}) = \\boxed{-4\\sqrt{2}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \\(-4\\sqrt{2}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(2\\sqrt{72} = 12\\sqrt{2}\\), और \\((3 - 2\\sqrt{2})^2 = 17 - 12\\sqrt{2}\\)<br>अतः \\(\\sqrt{17 - 12\\sqrt{2}} = 3 - 2\\sqrt{2}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{3 - 2\\sqrt{2}} = 3 + 2\\sqrt{2}\\)<br>व्यंजक = \\((3 - 2\\sqrt{2}) - (3 + 2\\sqrt{2}) = \\boxed{-4\\sqrt{2}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \\(-4\\sqrt{2}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000075141","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A tent, 17 m high, is shaped as a frustum of a cone topped with a hemisphere. The diameters of the top and bottom circular ends of the frustum are 16 m and 40 m, respectively. Calculate the surface area of the cloth required to make the tent, ignoring any wastage. (Use π = 22/7) [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"17 m ऊँचा एक तंबू शंकु के छिन्नक के रूप में है जिसके ऊपर एक अर्धगोला है। छिन्नक के ऊपरी और निचले वृत्तीय सिरों के व्यास क्रमशः 16 m और 40 m हैं। बिना किसी बर्बादी के तंबू बनाने के लिए आवश्यक कपड़े का पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल ज्ञात कीजिए। (π = 22/7 लीजिए) [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1810.34 m²"},"2":{"en":"1936.12 m²"},"3":{"en":"1722.29 m²"},"4":{"en":"1614.46 m²"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Hemisphere radius = top radius = \\(\\frac{16}{2} = 8\\) m, bottom radius = \\(\\frac{40}{2} = 20\\) m<br>Frustum height = \\(17 - 8 = 9\\) m; slant height \\(l = \\sqrt{9^2 + (20-8)^2} = \\sqrt{81 + 144} = 15\\) m<br>Curved surface of frustum = \\(\\pi(r_1 + r_2)l = \\frac{22}{7} \\times 28 \\times 15 = 1320\\) m²<br>Curved surface of hemisphere = \\(2\\pi r^2 = 2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 64 = 402.29\\) m²<br>Total cloth = \\(1320 + 402.29 = \\boxed{1722.29}\\) m²<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 1722.29 m².</b>","hi":"अर्धगोले की त्रिज्या = ऊपरी त्रिज्या = \\(\\frac{16}{2} = 8\\) m, निचली त्रिज्या = \\(\\frac{40}{2} = 20\\) m<br>छिन्नक की ऊँचाई = \\(17 - 8 = 9\\) m; तिर्यक ऊँचाई \\(l = \\sqrt{9^2 + (20-8)^2} = \\sqrt{81 + 144} = 15\\) m<br>छिन्नक का वक्र पृष्ठ = \\(\\pi(r_1 + r_2)l = \\frac{22}{7} \\times 28 \\times 15 = 1320\\) m²<br>अर्धगोले का वक्र पृष्ठ = \\(2\\pi r^2 = 2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 64 = 402.29\\) m²<br>कुल कपड़ा = \\(1320 + 402.29 = \\boxed{1722.29}\\) m²<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 1722.29 m² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000075142","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"A perpendicular of length 15 cm is drawn from the centre of a circle to a chord of length 40 cm. Find the radius of the circle. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक वृत्त के केंद्र से 40 cm लंबी जीवा पर 15 cm लंबा लंब खींचा जाता है। वृत्त की त्रिज्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20 cm"},"2":{"en":"22 cm"},"3":{"en":"25 cm"},"4":{"en":"27 cm"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The perpendicular from the centre bisects the chord: half chord = \\(\\frac{40}{2} = 20\\) cm<br>Radius = \\(\\sqrt{15^2 + 20^2} = \\sqrt{225 + 400}\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{625} = \\boxed{25}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 25 cm.</b>","hi":"केंद्र से डाला गया लंब जीवा को समद्विभाजित करता है: आधी जीवा = \\(\\frac{40}{2} = 20\\) cm<br>त्रिज्या = \\(\\sqrt{15^2 + 20^2} = \\sqrt{225 + 400}\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{625} = \\boxed{25}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 25 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000075143","section":"MATH","topic":"Set Relation and Function","question":{"en":"The algebraic numbers A form a subfield of C. What is the cardinality of A? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"बीजगणितीय संख्याएँ A, C का उपक्षेत्र बनाती हैं। A की गणन-संख्या (cardinality) क्या है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Finite.","hi":"परिमित।"},"2":{"en":"Countably infinite.","hi":"गणनीय रूप से अनंत।"},"3":{"en":"Uncountably infinite, same cardinality as R.","hi":"अगणनीय रूप से अनंत, R के समान गणन-संख्या।"},"4":{"en":"Strictly between |N| and |R|.","hi":"|N| और |R| के बीच।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Every algebraic number is a root of some non-zero polynomial with rational coefficients.<br>There are only countably many such polynomials, and each has finitely many roots, so A is a countable union of finite sets.<br>Hence A is \\(\\boxed{\\text{Countably infinite}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Countably infinite..</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक बीजगणितीय संख्या किसी शून्येतर परिमेय गुणांक वाले बहुपद का मूल होती है।<br>ऐसे बहुपद केवल गणनीय रूप से अनेक हैं और प्रत्येक के परिमित मूल होते हैं, अतः A परिमित समुच्चयों का गणनीय संघ है।<br>इसलिए A \\(\\boxed{\\text{गणनीय रूप से अनंत}}\\) है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): गणनीय रूप से अनंत। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000075144","section":"MATH","topic":"Set Relation and Function","question":{"en":"Consider the field extension (Q(√2, √3)/Q). Its degree [Q(√2, √3) : Q] equals: [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"क्षेत्र विस्तार (Q(√2, √3)/Q) पर विचार कीजिए। इसकी घात [Q(√2, √3) : Q] बराबर है: [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2"},"2":{"en":"3"},"3":{"en":"4"},"4":{"en":"8"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\([\\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{2}) : \\mathbb{Q}] = 2\\) with minimal polynomial \\(x^2 - 2\\)<br>Over \\(\\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{2})\\), the polynomial \\(x^2 - 3\\) stays irreducible, so the next layer also has degree 2<br>\\([\\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{2}, \\sqrt{3}) : \\mathbb{Q}] = 2 \\times 2 = \\boxed{4}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 4.</b>","hi":"\\([\\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{2}) : \\mathbb{Q}] = 2\\), न्यूनतम बहुपद \\(x^2 - 2\\) के साथ<br>\\(\\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{2})\\) के ऊपर बहुपद \\(x^2 - 3\\) अखंडनीय रहता है, अतः अगली परत की घात भी 2 है<br>\\([\\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{2}, \\sqrt{3}) : \\mathbb{Q}] = 2 \\times 2 = \\boxed{4}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 4 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000075145","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"Simplify the expression: \\(\\sqrt{16 + 6\\sqrt{2} + 6\\sqrt{5} + 2\\sqrt{10}}\\) [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"व्यंजक को सरल कीजिए: \\(\\sqrt{16 + 6\\sqrt{2} + 6\\sqrt{5} + 2\\sqrt{10}}\\) [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{5} + 3\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{5} - 3\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{2} - \\sqrt{5} + 3\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{2} - \\sqrt{5} - 3\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Try \\((\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{5} + 3)^2\\):<br>\\(= 2 + 5 + 9 + 2\\sqrt{10} + 6\\sqrt{2} + 6\\sqrt{5}\\)<br>\\(= 16 + 6\\sqrt{2} + 6\\sqrt{5} + 2\\sqrt{10}\\)<br>So the square root is \\(\\boxed{\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{5} + 3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{5} + 3\\).</b>","hi":"\\((\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{5} + 3)^2\\) पर विचार कीजिए:<br>\\(= 2 + 5 + 9 + 2\\sqrt{10} + 6\\sqrt{2} + 6\\sqrt{5}\\)<br>\\(= 16 + 6\\sqrt{2} + 6\\sqrt{5} + 2\\sqrt{10}\\)<br>अतः वर्गमूल \\(\\boxed{\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{5} + 3}\\) है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{5} + 3\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000075146","section":"MATH","topic":"Simple Interest (SI)","question":{"en":"A farmer borrows ₹2,00,000 at simple interest. After 9 years, he repays a total amount of ₹2,88,000 to fully settle the loan. If another farmer borrows ₹3,00,000 at the same rate for 15 years, how much more interest would he pay compared to the first farmer? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक किसान साधारण ब्याज पर ₹2,00,000 उधार लेता है। 9 वर्षों बाद वह ऋण पूरी तरह चुकाने के लिए कुल ₹2,88,000 लौटाता है। यदि दूसरा किसान उसी दर पर 15 वर्षों के लिए ₹3,00,000 उधार लेता है, तो वह पहले किसान की तुलना में कितना अधिक ब्याज देगा? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹1,32,000"},"2":{"en":"₹1,34,000"},"3":{"en":"₹1,39,000"},"4":{"en":"₹1,44,000"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Interest of the first farmer = \\(2{,}88{,}000 - 2{,}00{,}000 = 88{,}000\\)<br>\\(88{,}000 = \\frac{2{,}00{,}000 \\times r \\times 9}{100} \\Rightarrow r = \\frac{88}{18}\\% = \\frac{44}{9}\\%\\)<br>Interest of the second farmer = \\(\\frac{3{,}00{,}000 \\times 44 \\times 15}{9 \\times 100} = 2{,}20{,}000\\)<br>Difference = \\(2{,}20{,}000 - 88{,}000 = \\boxed{1{,}32{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): ₹1,32,000.</b>","hi":"पहले किसान का ब्याज = \\(2{,}88{,}000 - 2{,}00{,}000 = 88{,}000\\)<br>\\(88{,}000 = \\frac{2{,}00{,}000 \\times r \\times 9}{100} \\Rightarrow r = \\frac{88}{18}\\% = \\frac{44}{9}\\%\\)<br>दूसरे किसान का ब्याज = \\(\\frac{3{,}00{,}000 \\times 44 \\times 15}{9 \\times 100} = 2{,}20{,}000\\)<br>अंतर = \\(2{,}20{,}000 - 88{,}000 = \\boxed{1{,}32{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): ₹1,32,000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000075147","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"Three liquids A, B and C are mixed in a vessel in the ratio 7 : 8 : 11, respectively. 1/3 rd of the mixture is then taken out of the vessel and kept aside for an experiment. 1/2 of the remaining quantity in the vessel gets accidentally spilled. Then, some quantity of liquid B is again added to the vessel so that the ratio of the three liquids in this new mixture becomes 7 : 12 : 11, respectively. If the quantity of the new mixture in the vessel is 60 ml, what was the quantity of the original mixture in the vessel at the beginning? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक बर्तन में तीन द्रव A, B और C क्रमशः 7 : 8 : 11 के अनुपात में मिलाए जाते हैं। फिर मिश्रण का 1/3 भाग बर्तन से निकालकर प्रयोग के लिए अलग रख दिया जाता है। बर्तन में शेष मात्रा का 1/2 भाग दुर्घटनावश बह जाता है। फिर बर्तन में कुछ मात्रा में द्रव B दोबारा मिलाया जाता है, जिससे नए मिश्रण में तीनों द्रवों का अनुपात क्रमशः 7 : 12 : 11 हो जाता है। यदि बर्तन में नए मिश्रण की मात्रा 60 ml है, तो शुरू में बर्तन में मूल मिश्रण की मात्रा कितनी थी? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"156 ml"},"2":{"en":"160 ml"},"3":{"en":"164 ml"},"4":{"en":"180 ml"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Let the original mixture be \\(26k\\) (A = 7k, B = 8k, C = 11k).<br>After removing 1/3, 2/3 remains: A = \\(\\frac{14k}{3}\\), B = \\(\\frac{16k}{3}\\), C = \\(\\frac{22k}{3}\\)<br>After half spills, half remains: A = \\(\\frac{7k}{3}\\), B = \\(\\frac{8k}{3}\\), C = \\(\\frac{11k}{3}\\)<br>A : C = 7 : 11 is unchanged, so with ratio 7 : 12 : 11 the final quantities are \\(\\frac{7k}{3}, 4k, \\frac{11k}{3}\\) (B added = \\(\\frac{4k}{3}\\))<br>Total = \\(\\frac{7k}{3} + 4k + \\frac{11k}{3} = 10k = 60 \\Rightarrow k = 6\\)<br>Original mixture = \\(26 \\times 6 = \\boxed{156}\\) ml<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 156 ml.</b>","hi":"मूल मिश्रण \\(26k\\) मानिए (A = 7k, B = 8k, C = 11k)<br>1/3 निकालने पर 2/3 बचता है: A = \\(\\frac{14k}{3}\\), B = \\(\\frac{16k}{3}\\), C = \\(\\frac{22k}{3}\\)<br>आधा बह जाने पर आधा बचता है: A = \\(\\frac{7k}{3}\\), B = \\(\\frac{8k}{3}\\), C = \\(\\frac{11k}{3}\\)<br>A : C = 7 : 11 अपरिवर्तित है, अतः 7 : 12 : 11 के अनुसार अंतिम मात्राएँ \\(\\frac{7k}{3}, 4k, \\frac{11k}{3}\\) हैं (B मिलाया = \\(\\frac{4k}{3}\\))<br>कुल = \\(\\frac{7k}{3} + 4k + \\frac{11k}{3} = 10k = 60 \\Rightarrow k = 6\\)<br>मूल मिश्रण = \\(26 \\times 6 = \\boxed{156}\\) ml<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 156 ml है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000075148","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If sinθ + cosecθ = 2, what is the value of \\(\\sin^n\\theta + \\csc^n\\theta\\) for any positive integer n? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि sinθ + cosecθ = 2 है, तो किसी भी धनात्मक पूर्णांक n के लिए \\(\\sin^n\\theta + \\csc^n\\theta\\) का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2"},"2":{"en":"\\(2^n\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(2^{n-1}\\)"},"4":{"en":"0"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Let \\(\\sin\\theta = t > 0\\). Then \\(t + \\frac{1}{t} = 2 \\Rightarrow t^2 - 2t + 1 = 0 \\Rightarrow (t - 1)^2 = 0\\)<br>So \\(\\sin\\theta = 1\\) and \\(\\csc\\theta = 1\\)<br>\\(\\sin^n\\theta + \\csc^n\\theta = 1 + 1 = \\boxed{2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 2.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए \\(\\sin\\theta = t > 0\\), तब \\(t + \\frac{1}{t} = 2 \\Rightarrow t^2 - 2t + 1 = 0 \\Rightarrow (t - 1)^2 = 0\\)<br>अतः \\(\\sin\\theta = 1\\) और \\(\\csc\\theta = 1\\)<br>\\(\\sin^n\\theta + \\csc^n\\theta = 1 + 1 = \\boxed{2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000075149","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"A mechanical arm in a robotic assembly line rotates through an angle of 3π/4 radians during a precise welding operation. What is the measure of this rotation angle in degrees? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"रोबोटिक असेंबली लाइन में एक यांत्रिक भुजा एक सटीक वेल्डिंग कार्य के दौरान 3π/4 रेडियन के कोण से घूमती है। इस घूर्णन कोण का माप डिग्री में क्या है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"120°"},"2":{"en":"135°"},"3":{"en":"145°"},"4":{"en":"150°"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\\) radians \\(= \\frac{3\\pi}{4} \\times \\frac{180^\\circ}{\\pi}\\)<br>\\(= 3 \\times 45^\\circ = \\boxed{135^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 135°.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\\) रेडियन \\(= \\frac{3\\pi}{4} \\times \\frac{180^\\circ}{\\pi}\\)<br>\\(= 3 \\times 45^\\circ = \\boxed{135^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 135° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000075150","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Simplify: \\(\\frac{\\sin 75^\\circ - \\sin 15^\\circ}{\\cos 15^\\circ - \\cos 75^\\circ}\\) [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"सरल कीजिए: \\(\\frac{\\sin 75^\\circ - \\sin 15^\\circ}{\\cos 15^\\circ - \\cos 75^\\circ}\\) [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"0"},"3":{"en":"sin 60°"},"4":{"en":"cos 60°"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sin 75^\\circ - \\sin 15^\\circ = 2\\cos 45^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\cos 15^\\circ - \\cos 75^\\circ = -2\\sin 45^\\circ \\sin(-30^\\circ) = 2\\sin 45^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ\\)<br>Since \\(\\cos 45^\\circ = \\sin 45^\\circ\\), the ratio is \\(\\frac{2\\cos 45^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ}{2\\sin 45^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ} = \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1.</b>","hi":"\\(\\sin 75^\\circ - \\sin 15^\\circ = 2\\cos 45^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\cos 15^\\circ - \\cos 75^\\circ = -2\\sin 45^\\circ \\sin(-30^\\circ) = 2\\sin 45^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ\\)<br>चूँकि \\(\\cos 45^\\circ = \\sin 45^\\circ\\), अनुपात = \\(\\frac{2\\cos 45^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ}{2\\sin 45^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ} = \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000075151","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If (a+b)² = 196 and (a−b)² = 36, find ab. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि (a+b)² = 196 और (a−b)² = 36 है, तो ab ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"32"},"2":{"en":"160"},"3":{"en":"40"},"4":{"en":"80"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\((a + b)^2 - (a - b)^2 = 4ab\\)<br>\\(196 - 36 = 160 = 4ab\\)<br>\\(ab = \\boxed{40}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 40.</b>","hi":"\\((a + b)^2 - (a - b)^2 = 4ab\\)<br>\\(196 - 36 = 160 = 4ab\\)<br>\\(ab = \\boxed{40}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 40 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000075152","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"From an external point P which is at a distance of 6 cm from the center O of a circle of radius 3 cm, a pair of tangents are drawn. Find the angle θ between the two tangents. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"3 cm त्रिज्या वाले वृत्त के केंद्र O से 6 cm दूर स्थित बाह्य बिंदु P से दो स्पर्श रेखाएँ खींची जाती हैं। दोनों स्पर्श रेखाओं के बीच का कोण θ ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"30°"},"2":{"en":"45°"},"3":{"en":"60°"},"4":{"en":"90°"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In the right triangle formed by the centre, the external point and the point of contact: \\(\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2} = \\frac{r}{OP}\\)<br>\\(\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2} = \\frac{3}{6} = \\frac{1}{2} \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\theta}{2} = 30^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\theta = \\boxed{60^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 60°.</b>","hi":"केंद्र, बाह्य बिंदु और स्पर्श बिंदु से बने समकोण त्रिभुज में: \\(\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2} = \\frac{r}{OP}\\)<br>\\(\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2} = \\frac{3}{6} = \\frac{1}{2} \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\theta}{2} = 30^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\theta = \\boxed{60^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 60° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000075153","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In ΔABC, D is the midpoint of side BC and E is the midpoint of side AC. The segments BE and AD intersect at point G. If the area of ΔBDG is 5 square units, find the area of ΔABC. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"ΔABC में, D भुजा BC का मध्यबिंदु और E भुजा AC का मध्यबिंदु है। रेखाखंड BE और AD बिंदु G पर प्रतिच्छेद करते हैं। यदि ΔBDG का क्षेत्रफल 5 वर्ग इकाई है, तो ΔABC का क्षेत्रफल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"30 square units","hi":"30 वर्ग इकाई"},"2":{"en":"45 square units","hi":"45 वर्ग इकाई"},"3":{"en":"60 square units","hi":"60 वर्ग इकाई"},"4":{"en":"75 square units","hi":"75 वर्ग इकाई"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"AD and BE are medians, so G is the centroid and divides each median in the ratio 2 : 1.<br>The three medians divide the triangle into six equal small triangles.<br>Area of ΔBDG = \\(\\frac{1}{6} \\times\\) area of ΔABC<br>Area of ΔABC = \\(6 \\times 5 = \\boxed{30}\\) square units<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 30 square units.</b>","hi":"AD और BE माध्यिकाएँ हैं, अतः G केंद्रक है और प्रत्येक माध्यिका को 2 : 1 में विभाजित करता है।<br>तीनों माध्यिकाएँ त्रिभुज को छह बराबर छोटे त्रिभुजों में बाँटती हैं।<br>ΔBDG का क्षेत्रफल = \\(\\frac{1}{6} \\times\\) ΔABC का क्षेत्रफल<br>ΔABC का क्षेत्रफल = \\(6 \\times 5 = \\boxed{30}\\) वर्ग इकाई<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 30 वर्ग इकाई है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000075154","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two separate circles have radii of 8 cm and 2 cm. If the distance between their centers is 13 cm, find the length of their transverse common tangent. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दो अलग वृत्तों की त्रिज्याएँ 8 cm और 2 cm हैं। यदि उनके केंद्रों के बीच की दूरी 13 cm है, तो उनकी तिर्यक उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"≈ 8.31 cm"},"2":{"en":"≈ 11.5 cm"},"3":{"en":"≈ 13.21 cm"},"4":{"en":"≈ 14.4 cm"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"For a transverse common tangent, length \\(= \\sqrt{d^2 - (r_1 + r_2)^2}\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{13^2 - (8 + 2)^2} = \\sqrt{169 - 100}\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{69} \\approx \\boxed{8.31}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): ≈ 8.31 cm.</b>","hi":"तिर्यक उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा के लिए, लंबाई \\(= \\sqrt{d^2 - (r_1 + r_2)^2}\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{13^2 - (8 + 2)^2} = \\sqrt{169 - 100}\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{69} \\approx \\boxed{8.31}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): ≈ 8.31 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000075155","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"A, B, C and D can complete a work individually in 16 days, 24 days, 48 days and 32 days, respectively. All four work together for 4 days. Thereafter A works at 75% of his original efficiency, B at 150%, C at 250% and D at 80%. How much total time, from the start, is required to complete the work? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"A, B, C और D किसी कार्य को अलग-अलग क्रमशः 16 दिन, 24 दिन, 48 दिन और 32 दिन में पूरा कर सकते हैं। चारों मिलकर 4 दिन कार्य करते हैं। इसके बाद A अपनी मूल क्षमता के 75% पर, B 150% पर, C 250% पर और D 80% पर कार्य करते हैं। शुरुआत से कार्य पूरा करने में कुल कितना समय लगेगा? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(5\\frac{173}{179}\\) days","hi":"\\(5\\frac{173}{179}\\) दिन"},"2":{"en":"6 days","hi":"6 दिन"},"3":{"en":"\\(6\\frac{1}{179}\\) days","hi":"\\(6\\frac{1}{179}\\) दिन"},"4":{"en":"\\(6\\frac{2}{179}\\) days","hi":"\\(6\\frac{2}{179}\\) दिन"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"One day's work of all four = \\(\\frac{1}{16} + \\frac{1}{24} + \\frac{1}{48} + \\frac{1}{32} = \\frac{6+4+2+3}{96} = \\frac{15}{96} = \\frac{5}{32}\\)<br>In 4 days = \\(\\frac{20}{32} = \\frac{5}{8}\\); work left = \\(\\frac{3}{8}\\)<br>New rates: A = \\(\\frac{3}{64}\\), B = \\(\\frac{1}{16}\\), C = \\(\\frac{5}{96}\\), D = \\(\\frac{1}{40}\\)<br>Sum = \\(\\frac{45 + 60 + 50 + 24}{960} = \\frac{179}{960}\\) per day<br>Time = \\(\\frac{3/8}{179/960} = \\frac{360}{179} = 2\\frac{2}{179}\\) days<br>Total time = \\(4 + 2\\frac{2}{179} = \\boxed{6\\frac{2}{179}}\\) days<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): \\(6\\frac{2}{179}\\) days.</b>","hi":"चारों का एक दिन का कार्य = \\(\\frac{1}{16} + \\frac{1}{24} + \\frac{1}{48} + \\frac{1}{32} = \\frac{6+4+2+3}{96} = \\frac{5}{32}\\)<br>4 दिनों में = \\(\\frac{20}{32} = \\frac{5}{8}\\); शेष कार्य = \\(\\frac{3}{8}\\)<br>नई दरें: A = \\(\\frac{3}{64}\\), B = \\(\\frac{1}{16}\\), C = \\(\\frac{5}{96}\\), D = \\(\\frac{1}{40}\\)<br>योग = \\(\\frac{45 + 60 + 50 + 24}{960} = \\frac{179}{960}\\) प्रति दिन<br>समय = \\(\\frac{3/8}{179/960} = \\frac{360}{179} = 2\\frac{2}{179}\\) दिन<br>कुल समय = \\(4 + 2\\frac{2}{179} = \\boxed{6\\frac{2}{179}}\\) दिन<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): \\(6\\frac{2}{179}\\) दिन है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000075156","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Convert the below given indirect speech into direct speech appropriately:<br>She said that she would visit the museum the next day. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"She said, “I will visit the museum tomorrow”."},"2":{"en":"She said, “She would visit the museum the next day”."},"3":{"en":"She said, “I am visiting the museum tomorrow”."},"4":{"en":"She said, “She would be visiting the museum the next day”."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Would” reverses to “will,” and “the next day” to “tomorrow.”</b><br>The reported “she” becomes “I.”<br>A restores the original future statement.<br>The other options retain reported forms or change the tense.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): She said, “I will visit the museum tomorrow”..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000075157","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Four parts of a sentence are given below in a jumbled order. When arranged correctly, they form a complete and meaningful sentence. While multiple combinations may appear grammatically correct, choose the one that best conveys the intended meaning as per the given options.<br>A) for climate adaptation<br>B) are being taken<br>C) several initiatives<br>D) by Indian cities [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A-B-C-D"},"2":{"en":"C-B-D-A"},"3":{"en":"D-C-B-A"},"4":{"en":"B-C-D-A"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: C-B-D-A</b><br>C supplies the subject, and B the present continuous passive predicate.<br>D identifies the actors: Indian cities.<br>A gives the purpose: climate adaptation.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): C-B-D-A.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000075158","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Four parts of a sentence are given below in a jumbled order. When arranged correctly, they form a complete and meaningful sentence. While multiple combinations may appear grammatically correct, choose the one that best conveys the intended meaning as per the given options.<br>A) to track delivery<br>B) of government schemes<br>C) a real-time dashboard<br>D) has been introduced [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"D-C-A-B"},"2":{"en":"A-B-C-D"},"3":{"en":"C-D-A-B"},"4":{"en":"B-D-C-A"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: C-D-A-B</b><br>C supplies the subject, and D the present perfect passive predicate.<br>A states the dashboard’s purpose: tracking delivery.<br>B completes what is delivered: government schemes.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): C-D-A-B.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000075159","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the correct collocation:<br>The NGO took ___ the responsibility of educating underprivileged children in rural areas. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"on"},"2":{"en":"in"},"3":{"en":"off"},"4":{"en":"out"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Take on (जिम्मेदारी लेना) = accept a duty or responsibility.</b><br>The NGO took on responsibility for educating rural children.<br>“Take in” means absorb or deceive, “take off” means depart.<br>“Take out” means remove.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): on.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000075160","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Choose the grammatically INCORRECT sentence. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The workers have been demanding their wages for over a month"},"2":{"en":"The newly built highway connects Delhi to Agra seamlessly"},"3":{"en":"She did not realise that she was supposed to submit the form by yesterday"},"4":{"en":"The committee have decided to postpone the event"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Committee” is treated as singular in the intended usage.</b><br>Correct sentence: “The committee <b>has</b> decided to postpone the event.”<br>The other sentences use acceptable verb forms and structures.<br>“By yesterday” is awkward but denotes the expected deadline.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): The committee have decided to postpone the event.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000075161","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage below carefully and answer the questions that follow. Each question is based on the information provided in the passage. Ensure that you answer according to the content of the passage.<br><br>In India’s rapidly urbanising economy, the gig workforce has emerged as a significant player. This workforce comprises freelancers, delivery personnel, ride-share drivers, and others working on a task-by-task basis. The flexibility offered by the gig economy appeals to the youth, especially those with limited formal education or who are unable to find full-time employment. Platforms like Swiggy, Zomato, Ola, and Urban Company have played a major role in creating gig-based opportunities. However, there is concern about job security, absence of social security benefits, and fluctuating income. Despite these challenges, gig work often serves as a stopgap for individuals between traditional jobs. Policymakers are beginning to explore frameworks for social protection of gig workers, acknowledging their contribution to the urban economy.<br><br><br>Who are considered part of the gig workforce? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Government employees"},"2":{"en":"Full-time corporate staff"},"3":{"en":"Freelancers and delivery workers"},"4":{"en":"Factory workers with pensions"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: The workforce comprises freelancers, delivery personnel and ride-share drivers.</b><br>They work on a task-by-task basis.<br>Government, corporate and pensioned factory jobs are traditional employment.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Freelancers and delivery workers.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000075162","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage below carefully and answer the questions that follow. Each question is based on the information provided in the passage. Ensure that you answer according to the content of the passage.<br><br>In India’s rapidly urbanising economy, the gig workforce has emerged as a significant player. This workforce comprises freelancers, delivery personnel, ride-share drivers, and others working on a task-by-task basis. The flexibility offered by the gig economy appeals to the youth, especially those with limited formal education or who are unable to find full-time employment. Platforms like Swiggy, Zomato, Ola, and Urban Company have played a major role in creating gig-based opportunities. However, there is concern about job security, absence of social security benefits, and fluctuating income. Despite these challenges, gig work often serves as a stopgap for individuals between traditional jobs. Policymakers are beginning to explore frameworks for social protection of gig workers, acknowledging their contribution to the urban economy.<br><br><br>What is one appealing aspect of gig work? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Job security"},"2":{"en":"Flexible work arrangements"},"3":{"en":"Fixed salary and security"},"4":{"en":"Guaranteed government employment"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: The flexibility of the gig economy appeals to the youth.</b><br>Job security and fixed salaries are identified as concerns, not attractions.<br>Gig platforms do not guarantee government employment.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Flexible work arrangements.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000075163","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage below carefully and answer the questions that follow. Each question is based on the information provided in the passage. Ensure that you answer according to the content of the passage.<br><br>In India’s rapidly urbanising economy, the gig workforce has emerged as a significant player. This workforce comprises freelancers, delivery personnel, ride-share drivers, and others working on a task-by-task basis. The flexibility offered by the gig economy appeals to the youth, especially those with limited formal education or who are unable to find full-time employment. Platforms like Swiggy, Zomato, Ola, and Urban Company have played a major role in creating gig-based opportunities. However, there is concern about job security, absence of social security benefits, and fluctuating income. Despite these challenges, gig work often serves as a stopgap for individuals between traditional jobs. Policymakers are beginning to explore frameworks for social protection of gig workers, acknowledging their contribution to the urban economy.<br><br><br>What problem is associated with gig work? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"No job security and inconsistent income"},"2":{"en":"Overstaffing in offices"},"3":{"en":"Too many holidays"},"4":{"en":"High retirement benefits"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: Concerns include job insecurity and fluctuating income.</b><br>The passage also notes absent social-security benefits.<br>Office overstaffing, holidays and retirement benefits are not discussed.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): No job security and inconsistent income.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000075164","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage below carefully and answer the questions that follow. Each question is based on the information provided in the passage. Ensure that you answer according to the content of the passage.<br><br>In India’s rapidly urbanising economy, the gig workforce has emerged as a significant player. This workforce comprises freelancers, delivery personnel, ride-share drivers, and others working on a task-by-task basis. The flexibility offered by the gig economy appeals to the youth, especially those with limited formal education or who are unable to find full-time employment. Platforms like Swiggy, Zomato, Ola, and Urban Company have played a major role in creating gig-based opportunities. However, there is concern about job security, absence of social security benefits, and fluctuating income. Despite these challenges, gig work often serves as a stopgap for individuals between traditional jobs. Policymakers are beginning to explore frameworks for social protection of gig workers, acknowledging their contribution to the urban economy.<br><br><br>How do policymakers plan to address gig workers’ issues? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Offering private jobs"},"2":{"en":"Ignoring their demands"},"3":{"en":"Cutting platform access"},"4":{"en":"Exploring social protection frameworks"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: Policymakers are exploring frameworks for social protection.</b><br>This acknowledges gig workers’ contribution to the urban economy.<br>The other options contradict or are absent from the passage.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Exploring social protection frameworks.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000075165","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage below carefully and answer the questions that follow. Each question is based on the information provided in the passage. Ensure that you answer according to the content of the passage.<br><br>In India’s rapidly urbanising economy, the gig workforce has emerged as a significant player. This workforce comprises freelancers, delivery personnel, ride-share drivers, and others working on a task-by-task basis. The flexibility offered by the gig economy appeals to the youth, especially those with limited formal education or who are unable to find full-time employment. Platforms like Swiggy, Zomato, Ola, and Urban Company have played a major role in creating gig-based opportunities. However, there is concern about job security, absence of social security benefits, and fluctuating income. Despite these challenges, gig work often serves as a stopgap for individuals between traditional jobs. Policymakers are beginning to explore frameworks for social protection of gig workers, acknowledging their contribution to the urban economy.<br><br><br>Which of these platforms is NOT mentioned as part of the gig economy in the passage? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ola"},"2":{"en":"Zomato"},"3":{"en":"Urban Company"},"4":{"en":"Flipkart"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: The named platforms are Swiggy, Zomato, Ola and Urban Company.</b><br>Flipkart is not mentioned.<br>The other three are explicitly listed.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Flipkart.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000075166","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom given below:<br>“Hit the roof” [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Achieve success"},"2":{"en":"Become very angry"},"3":{"en":"Climb a building"},"4":{"en":"Escape trouble"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Hit the roof (बहुत क्रोधित होना) = become extremely angry.</b><br>Example: “Dad hit the roof when he saw the bill.”<br>Success, literal climbing and escaping trouble are unrelated.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Become very angry.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000075167","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Choose the correctly spelt word that best completes the sentence meaningfully.<br>The ___ for the new building will be presented to the committee next week. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"bleprint"},"2":{"en":"bluepring"},"3":{"en":"blueprint"},"4":{"en":"bluprint"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Blueprint (रुपरेखा) = a detailed design or plan.</b><br>The correct spelling is “blueprint.”<br><b>Bleprint</b> omits “u”; <b>bluepring</b> uses “g” instead of “t.”<br><b>Bluprint</b> omits “e.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): blueprint.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000075168","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Find the part of the sentence that contains an error:<br>The committee discussed about the proposal (1)/ for over two hours (2)/ but failed to reach (3)/ any conclusion. (4) [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(1)"},"2":{"en":"(2)"},"3":{"en":"(3)"},"4":{"en":"(4)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Discuss” is transitive and is not followed by “about.”</b><br>Part (1) should read “The committee <b>discussed the proposal</b>.”<br>“Talked about the proposal” would also be correct.<br>The other parts are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): (1).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000075169","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Select the correct one-word substitution for:<br>A speech delivered without preparation. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Monologue"},"2":{"en":"Memorised"},"3":{"en":"Prepared"},"4":{"en":"Impromptu"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Impromptu (बिना तैयारी का) = done without preparation.</b><br><b>Monologue (एकालाप)</b> = long speech by one person<br><b>Memorised</b> = learned by heart<br><b>Prepared</b> = arranged in advance<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Impromptu.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000075170","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"What does the idiom “To add fuel to the fire” mean? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To improve a situation"},"2":{"en":"To stop a situation from escalating"},"3":{"en":"To make a bad situation worse"},"4":{"en":"To remain neutral in a conflict"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Add fuel to the fire (आग में घी डालना) = worsen a conflict or problem.</b><br>Example: “His sarcastic reply added fuel to the fire.”<br>Improving, calming and remaining neutral are opposite ideas.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): To make a bad situation worse.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000075171","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"What does the idiom “To call it a day” mean? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To stop working for the day"},"2":{"en":"To make a decision"},"3":{"en":"To continue working after a break"},"4":{"en":"To start a new project"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Call it a day (दिन का काम समाप्त करना) = stop working.</b><br>Example: “We finished the draft, so let’s call it a day.”<br>It does not mean continuing or starting work.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): To stop working for the day.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000075172","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Which of the following is NOT a misspelt word? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Accomadation"},"2":{"en":"Accommodation"},"3":{"en":"Accommodetion"},"4":{"en":"Accomodation"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Accommodation (आवास) = lodging or a place to stay.</b><br>Only “accommodation,” with double “c” and double “m,” is correct.<br><b>Accomadation</b> omits “m”; <b>accommodetion</b> inserts “e.”<br><b>Accomodation</b> omits “m.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Accommodation.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000075173","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the underlined part of the sentence. If the sentence is already correct, select “No substitution required”.<br>Of all the candidates, he was the <b>most cleverest</b>. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"most clever"},"2":{"en":"more clever"},"3":{"en":"cleverest"},"4":{"en":"No substitution required"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Do not combine “most” with a superlative ending in “-est.”</b><br>“The cleverest” already expresses the superlative.<br>“Most clever” would be an alternative only without “-est.”<br>“More clever” is comparative and does not fit “of all.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): cleverest.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000075174","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the underlined part of the sentence:<br>The medicine must be taken <b>between 6 to 8 pm</b>. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"from 6 to 8 pm"},"2":{"en":"between 6 and 8 pm"},"3":{"en":"during 6-8 pm"},"4":{"en":"in 6 to 8 pm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Between” is paired with “and.”</b><br>Correct wording: “between 6 <b>and</b> 8 pm.”<br>“From … to” is also generally valid but the keyed replacement preserves “between.”<br>The other prepositions do not fit as precisely.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): between 6 and 8 pm.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000075175","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Change the following from active to passive:<br>They had been considering alternative solutions before the consultant arrived. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Alternative solutions were considered before the consultant arrived."},"2":{"en":"Alternative solutions had been being considered before the consultant arrived."},"3":{"en":"Alternative solutions had been considered before the arrival."},"4":{"en":"Alternative solutions were being considered before arrival."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Past perfect continuous passive = had been being + past participle.</b><br>The object “alternative solutions” becomes the subject.<br>B retains the continuous aspect and the complete time clause.<br>The other options change the aspect or omit details.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Alternative solutions had been being considered before the consultant arrived..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000075176","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Change the following from active to passive:<br>The editor was reviewing the final draft when the system crashed. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The final draft is reviewed by the editor."},"2":{"en":"The final draft was reviewed before the system crashed."},"3":{"en":"The final draft was being reviewed by the editor when the system crashed."},"4":{"en":"The final draft had been reviewed when the crash occurred."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Past continuous passive = was/were being + past participle.</b><br>The singular object “draft” takes “was being reviewed.”<br>The agent and the “when” clause remain unchanged.<br>The other options alter the tense or sequence.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): The final draft was being reviewed by the editor when the system crashed..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000075177","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"A sentence is provided in indirect speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding direct speech.<br>The coordinator instructed the volunteers to remain at their assigned stations until further orders were issued. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"“Remain at your posts until you receive further orders,” the coordinator said."},"2":{"en":"“Do not leave your stations unless instructed,” said the coordinator."},"3":{"en":"“You're to stay where assigned until the next announcement,” she said."},"4":{"en":"“All volunteers must stay put until they hear otherwise,” the coordinator said."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: An instruction becomes a direct imperative with the original duration.</b><br>A retains “remain,” the assigned posts and “until … further orders.”<br>B omits the explicit waiting period, and C substitutes an announcement.<br>D changes the instruction to a general obligation.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): “Remain at your posts until you receive further orders,” the coordinator said..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000075178","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful passage.<br>1. After encoding, the video file is compressed.<br>2. Compression reduces file size for web streaming.<br>3. The original video is first trimmed and edited.<br>4. It is then encoded into a preferred format. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3-1-4-2"},"2":{"en":"1-2-3-4"},"3":{"en":"4-3-1-2"},"4":{"en":"3-4-1-2"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 3-4-1-2</b><br>The original video is edited and then encoded.<br>After encoding, it is compressed.<br>The purpose of compression—smaller files for streaming—comes last.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 3-4-1-2.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000075179","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct one-word substitute for: “A situation involving mutually destructive conflict”. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Impasse"},"2":{"en":"Quagmire"},"3":{"en":"Pyrrhic"},"4":{"en":"Stalemate"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Pyrrhic (पिरिक) = involving devastating costs to both sides or to the victor.</b><br>A Pyrrhic conflict leaves the parties severely damaged.<br><b>Impasse</b> and <b>stalemate</b> = deadlock<br><b>Quagmire</b> = difficult, entangling situation<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Pyrrhic.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000075180","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"The following sentence has been divided into four parts (P, Q, R, and S). The last part (S5) is fixed. Rearrange the remaining parts to form a grammatically correct and meaningful sentence, and choose the correct sequence.<br>S1: There is in the British Museum a monument which was discovered<br>P: in 1838 called “The Harpy Monument,” which is thought to have been made<br>Q: in 500 B.C. and consists of a tower where a white marble frieze is let into the<br>R: sandstone frieze running round all four sides at a height of about twenty-one feet<br>S: from the ground, a design reflecting that the Lycians, in whose country it was found<br>S5: were accustomed to bury their dead at the top of such towers. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QRSP"},"2":{"en":"RSQP"},"3":{"en":"PQRS"},"4":{"en":"SPRQ"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: PQRS</b><br>P completes the discovery date and introduces the monument’s estimated creation.<br>Q supplies the date and tower description.<br>R and S describe the frieze’s height and lead into the burial custom in S5.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): PQRS.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};